1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:02,268
It's 21 to 20, a one-point difference.

2
00:00:02,869 --> 00:00:04,403
We just need one more point.

3
00:00:06,039 --> 00:00:07,740
They're going to run the same play.

4
00:00:07,741 --> 00:00:08,841
Watch out for number three.

5
00:00:09,643 --> 00:00:10,843
Keep your eyes on number three!

6
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:21,721
(Number three again, as expected)

7
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:23,656
Okay!

8
00:00:25,325 --> 00:00:28,394
(Off the arm, it's out.)

9
00:00:28,995 --> 00:00:32,597
(So close)

10
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:38,503
My bad, Myoung Hwa.

11
00:00:39,439 --> 00:00:40,706
It's 22 to 20.

12
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:42,341
(Third set, Shujitsu High School 22
: Wonder Dogs 20)

13
00:00:45,011 --> 00:00:46,445
Chae Rim receives. Jin attacks.

14
00:00:48,148 --> 00:00:49,281
But it's dug up.

15
00:00:51,184 --> 00:00:52,050
A tip.

16
00:00:53,987 --> 00:00:54,888
They saved it!

17
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:56,322
Free ball!

18
00:00:56,323 --> 00:00:58,224
(Shujitsu High's free ball)

19
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:00,292
Where will she aim?
(Where will the ball land?)

20
00:01:01,595 --> 00:01:02,628
Number one.

21
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:05,964
(Number one, as expected again)

22
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,066
Right-side attack!

23
00:01:08,244 --> 00:01:09,711
- Off the block and out!
- Exactly.

24
00:01:09,736 --> 00:01:12,805
They're trying to avoid sending it
to Myung Hwa's side...

25
00:01:12,939 --> 00:01:15,741
- by changing the toss at the last second.
- That's correct.

26
00:01:16,376 --> 00:01:17,843
Why can't we make that play?

27
00:01:18,111 --> 00:01:20,379
We might not win this.

28
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:24,149
I could feel myself running out of energy
as the game went on.

29
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:27,386
- They must be feeling tired by now.
- Yes.

30
00:01:27,887 --> 00:01:30,822
Guys, stay strong. We just need one point.

31
00:01:31,625 --> 00:01:34,126
Don't lose focus! Hang in there!

32
00:01:34,127 --> 00:01:35,761
Yes, stay focused!

33
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:37,730
You can do this, guys!

34
00:01:37,964 --> 00:01:39,564
Keep your energy up!

35
00:01:39,566 --> 00:01:41,700
(We can't lose like this.)

36
00:01:44,371 --> 00:01:47,206
(Calling for a substitution)

37
00:01:47,907 --> 00:01:50,075
Young In and Na Yeon are
back on the court.

38
00:01:50,076 --> 00:01:52,110
(Jin out, Na Yeon in)

39
00:01:53,246 --> 00:01:58,317
(Will the rookie coach's substitution call
change the flow of the game?)

40
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:03,622
(Na Yeon, newly sent in, serves.)

41
00:02:07,594 --> 00:02:09,461
(Serve error)

42
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:12,831
(Squeezing eyes shut)

43
00:02:12,832 --> 00:02:13,899
A serve error.

44
00:02:18,204 --> 00:02:19,838
I'm sorry. My bad.

45
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:25,611
(Only one point away
from Shujitsu High winning the third set)

46
00:02:26,079 --> 00:02:27,813
(Let's go!)

47
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:29,548
(Go, Shujitsu High!)

48
00:02:29,949 --> 00:02:30,916
Go again!

49
00:02:32,752 --> 00:02:34,519
Just one point, please!

50
00:02:35,422 --> 00:02:38,591
(Third set, Shujitsu High School 24
: Wonder Dogs 22)

51
00:02:38,692 --> 00:02:40,593
Look out for player number one.
Number one!

52
00:02:50,704 --> 00:02:51,637
Look out.

53
00:02:52,806 --> 00:02:55,608
(Number one's attack coming!)

54
00:03:00,714 --> 00:03:01,847
Middle attack!

55
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:03,515
Set over!

56
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:04,616
Go!

57
00:03:09,522 --> 00:03:12,324
(Ace Miharu's deadly spike)

58
00:03:12,826 --> 00:03:14,593
The third set is over.

59
00:03:14,594 --> 00:03:15,694
(Third set, Shujitsu High School 25
: Wonder Dogs 22)

60
00:03:15,695 --> 00:03:17,062
The score is 25 to 22.

61
00:03:17,464 --> 00:03:20,633
Shujitsu High takes the victory
in the third set.

62
00:03:21,568 --> 00:03:23,435
The one and only Shujitsu High.

63
00:03:24,003 --> 00:03:27,806
As the champion among
Japanese high school volleyball teams,

64
00:03:28,608 --> 00:03:30,208
they're not going down easily.

65
00:03:33,813 --> 00:03:34,980
We still have a chance.

66
00:03:35,115 --> 00:03:37,616
So many errors from the beginning.

67
00:03:37,617 --> 00:03:39,785
We've had some disappointing plays.

68
00:03:40,453 --> 00:03:42,921
What was that last serve?
It wasn't even a strong one.

69
00:03:50,663 --> 00:03:52,831
We have to push harder in this set.

70
00:03:53,032 --> 00:03:55,600
Do you really want
to make our lives harder?

71
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:57,135
- No.
- I get it.

72
00:03:57,136 --> 00:04:00,572
I get that you're trying your hardest
to get one or two points,

73
00:04:00,774 --> 00:04:03,709
but you have to strike with full power.

74
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:05,411
- Don't hold back.
- Got it.

75
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:06,478
I get it.

76
00:04:06,479 --> 00:04:07,479
No, listen.

77
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:08,947
No, listen.

78
00:04:09,382 --> 00:04:11,083
Look, Chae Rim and Young In.

79
00:04:11,084 --> 00:04:12,985
Which part of their block was low?

80
00:04:12,986 --> 00:04:15,154
- Side.
- That's right.

81
00:04:15,154 --> 00:04:17,222
So why did you keep
attacking the middle...

82
00:04:17,223 --> 00:04:19,458
and miss the opportunity to score?
Hit the low spot.

83
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:21,994
Just hit the ball straight.
The libero wasn't even there to defend.

84
00:04:21,995 --> 00:04:23,062
- Okay.
- You get it?

85
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:25,664
- We won the first two sets, guys.
- Right.

86
00:04:25,665 --> 00:04:28,400
Let's go back to the basics
and build from there.

87
00:04:28,401 --> 00:04:30,102
Let's do this, guys!

88
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,470
Let's do this!

89
00:04:31,471 --> 00:04:33,639
- Let's go!
- Yes, let's go!

90
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:34,874
- One, two, three. Go!
- Go!

91
00:04:34,874 --> 00:04:36,675
(Let's try again!)

92
00:04:36,709 --> 00:04:39,177
Let's get locked in early! Stay sharp!

93
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:40,979
Come on, guys!

94
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:42,747
Let's do this! Let's take the lead!

95
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:46,252
After dropping the third set,
the score is now two to one.

96
00:04:46,853 --> 00:04:48,854
The fourth set kicks off
with Seung Ju's serve.

97
00:04:49,389 --> 00:04:50,189
(Shaky)
The ball's back over.

98
00:04:52,225 --> 00:04:53,692
Come on, make a good receive!

99
00:04:53,693 --> 00:04:54,594
Young In!
(Remember what we talked about?)

100
00:04:55,728 --> 00:04:57,662
(Hit it hard!)

101
00:04:57,664 --> 00:04:58,464
Hit it!

102
00:05:03,310 --> 00:05:04,910
Young In spikes, and they dig it up.

103
00:05:06,773 --> 00:05:08,741
(Shujitsu High sends it back in a hurry.)

104
00:05:08,942 --> 00:05:09,775
Free ball!

105
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:14,680
(Left side, Chae Rim's ball)

106
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:16,815
Hit it deep. Go long!

107
00:05:16,884 --> 00:05:18,417
I believed in myself.

108
00:05:18,685 --> 00:05:20,486
I promised myself I'd win.

109
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,787
Chae Rim's spike!

110
00:05:23,122 --> 00:05:24,522
It's a touch out.

111
00:05:24,524 --> 00:05:25,491
(Touch out right away.)

112
00:05:26,092 --> 00:05:27,693
(Chae Rim scores with a powerful spike.)

113
00:05:27,827 --> 00:05:28,727
Nice!

114
00:05:28,962 --> 00:05:30,329
Number six and number one!

115
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,797
(That's it! Nice spike.)

116
00:05:32,298 --> 00:05:33,698
Sorry.

117
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,400
It's zero to one.

118
00:05:35,401 --> 00:05:36,901
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 0
: Wonder Dogs 1)

119
00:05:36,903 --> 00:05:38,003
One, two, three.

120
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,805
- Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

121
00:05:45,478 --> 00:05:46,445
They pass it.

122
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,280
(My ball!)

123
00:05:50,984 --> 00:05:51,951
Myung Hwa's block.

124
00:05:54,921 --> 00:05:55,754
(Not even a chance.)

125
00:05:55,755 --> 00:05:57,856
- Seung Ju makes the receive!
- Hit it!

126
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:59,725
(The ball is back to Chae Rim.)

127
00:05:59,893 --> 00:06:00,693
Hit it!

128
00:06:01,427 --> 00:06:03,595
Spike! Chae Rim scores!

129
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:07,632
Chae Rim hits the ball diagonally...

130
00:06:07,634 --> 00:06:10,336
- twice in a row and scores both times.
- That's right.

131
00:06:10,603 --> 00:06:11,736
Nice defense, Seung Ju!

132
00:06:11,738 --> 00:06:13,205
(Another key player, Seung Ju)

133
00:06:13,206 --> 00:06:14,807
Nice defense, Seung Ju.

134
00:06:15,808 --> 00:06:16,841
One, two, three.

135
00:06:16,843 --> 00:06:18,343
- Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

136
00:06:22,415 --> 00:06:23,982
(Another shaky receive!)

137
00:06:28,421 --> 00:06:31,623
Seung Ju scores with her serve!

138
00:06:31,624 --> 00:06:33,158
Okay! Yes!

139
00:06:35,261 --> 00:06:37,829
Seung Ju takes control
of the game completely!

140
00:06:38,097 --> 00:06:38,997
Nice serve!

141
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:41,633
Chae Rim!

142
00:06:42,335 --> 00:06:43,935
Spike, and they pass it.

143
00:06:44,830 --> 00:06:46,831
The ball hits the net and drops!

144
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:49,242
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

145
00:06:49,243 --> 00:06:50,009
Keep it up!

146
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:52,811
Finally, we strike first.

147
00:06:53,179 --> 00:06:54,780
It's four to one now.

148
00:06:56,015 --> 00:06:58,216
(Lips drying)

149
00:06:59,852 --> 00:07:02,454
Their number eight player always...

150
00:07:02,455 --> 00:07:05,857
- goes cross-court when we jump high.
- Yes, coach.

151
00:07:08,028 --> 00:07:08,994
Chae Rim!

152
00:07:10,463 --> 00:07:13,731
Chae Rim! Hit it straight!

153
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,767
You already scored
with the same play earlier!

154
00:07:16,302 --> 00:07:17,636
You already tried it once.

155
00:07:17,637 --> 00:07:19,338
You think they'll let it happen again?

156
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:20,640
No, coach.

157
00:07:22,642 --> 00:07:23,542
Na Yeon.

158
00:07:23,543 --> 00:07:24,910
(Na Yeon, come here for a second.)

159
00:07:24,911 --> 00:07:27,346
Don't pass it to Chae Rim's side.

160
00:07:27,346 --> 00:07:29,347
- Use Young In more.
- You want me to pass it to her?

161
00:07:29,348 --> 00:07:30,682
Yes, she's not in the rhythm,

162
00:07:30,683 --> 00:07:32,617
so try setting it to Young In more now.

163
00:07:35,555 --> 00:07:37,823
(Switching to Young In
as the main attack option)

164
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:39,892
Myung Hwa serving.

165
00:07:45,031 --> 00:07:46,031
A shaky receive.

166
00:07:46,265 --> 00:07:48,399
(Managing to save it somehow)

167
00:07:48,868 --> 00:07:50,235
Come on, Na Yeon.

168
00:07:50,236 --> 00:07:51,036
(Let's go, Na Yeon.)

169
00:07:51,037 --> 00:07:52,337
(Glancing)

170
00:07:54,707 --> 00:07:55,740
A surprise back set.

171
00:07:56,743 --> 00:07:58,510
(Oh, no.)

172
00:07:59,045 --> 00:08:00,012
Young In.

173
00:08:00,246 --> 00:08:01,213
Hit it!

174
00:08:03,016 --> 00:08:04,316
Spike!

175
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:07,419
I can't believe they saved that.

176
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,990
Young In, a follow-up tip!

177
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:14,126
Back to Young In again.

178
00:08:19,832 --> 00:08:22,367
Young In's setter dump, and score!

179
00:08:22,368 --> 00:08:24,536
(A successful surprise setter dump)

180
00:08:24,537 --> 00:08:27,274
Coach Yeon Koung's tactic works perfectly.

181
00:08:27,274 --> 00:08:28,206
(A perfect call)

182
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:30,976
Young In, nice play.

183
00:08:30,977 --> 00:08:32,778
Guys, let's push it more.

184
00:08:32,779 --> 00:08:33,980
(Now the right side's broken open!)

185
00:08:35,148 --> 00:08:36,915
(Another free ball for Wonder Dogs)

186
00:08:36,916 --> 00:08:38,250
No choice but to send it over.

187
00:08:38,918 --> 00:08:39,751
Mine!

188
00:08:39,886 --> 00:08:40,987
Yes, go!

189
00:08:40,987 --> 00:08:42,086
Na Yeon!

190
00:08:42,889 --> 00:08:44,556
Set it to Young In.

191
00:08:45,558 --> 00:08:48,226
(Back to Young In again)

192
00:08:50,797 --> 00:08:52,064
Young In spikes!

193
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:55,667
It drops inside the line!

194
00:08:55,668 --> 00:08:58,471
(Yes, Young In!)

195
00:08:58,871 --> 00:08:59,838
(Our clutch player!)

196
00:08:59,839 --> 00:09:01,907
Nice job, Young In. Nice play.

197
00:09:02,575 --> 00:09:04,042
It's eight to two now.

198
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:06,278
The Wonder Dogs are
completely dominating the game!

199
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:07,179
Let's go, guys!

200
00:09:12,278 --> 00:09:13,345
Young In serving.

201
00:09:18,295 --> 00:09:19,359
In the middle!

202
00:09:21,584 --> 00:09:24,019
(Defense fail)

203
00:09:27,747 --> 00:09:30,282
The score difference seems safe for now,

204
00:09:30,307 --> 00:09:32,008
but it's important to maintain it.

205
00:09:32,009 --> 00:09:33,009
That's right.

206
00:09:37,347 --> 00:09:40,316
(Uchida Riona's serve)

207
00:09:44,988 --> 00:09:46,922
(Serve ace)

208
00:09:46,923 --> 00:09:48,891
- It's in.
- That was a good serve.

209
00:09:51,361 --> 00:09:52,731
I'm sorry.

210
00:09:52,756 --> 00:09:54,197
(A brief lapse in focus
costs them a point.)

211
00:09:57,201 --> 00:09:58,635
(They're on fire.)

212
00:09:58,635 --> 00:10:00,936
- The serve was incredible.
- That's right.

213
00:10:01,071 --> 00:10:02,772
A serve ace by Riona.

214
00:10:02,773 --> 00:10:05,708
(Uchida Riona's second consecutive serve)

215
00:10:06,009 --> 00:10:08,077
Don't let the serve shake you.

216
00:10:08,350 --> 00:10:09,283
Watch out for your steps.

217
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:17,920
The reception is unsteady.

218
00:10:17,921 --> 00:10:18,921
Get it!

219
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:20,790
Get it!

220
00:10:20,791 --> 00:10:22,258
That's another serve ace!

221
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:25,828
(They've lost three points already.)

222
00:10:26,997 --> 00:10:28,097
I'm sorry.

223
00:10:28,098 --> 00:10:32,702
At this rate,
the opponent can easily catch up...

224
00:10:32,912 --> 00:10:35,747
and it'll give them all the momentum.

225
00:10:35,772 --> 00:10:36,705
Right.

226
00:10:37,374 --> 00:10:44,146
(Let's go, Rei!)

227
00:10:44,916 --> 00:10:49,018
Her serve is really powerful and sharp.

228
00:10:49,686 --> 00:10:52,154
Riona is a tenth grader.

229
00:10:57,227 --> 00:10:58,194
Let's block this one.
Mine.

230
00:10:59,029 --> 00:11:01,097
(Their reception is shaking again.)

231
00:11:01,098 --> 00:11:02,131
Will it be a serve ace again?

232
00:11:03,166 --> 00:11:04,800
They rush the ball over the net.

233
00:11:06,770 --> 00:11:07,703
It's a fake set.

234
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:12,074
It goes over to the opponent's court!

235
00:11:12,075 --> 00:11:14,076
It's a chance!

236
00:11:15,579 --> 00:11:16,512
Smash!

237
00:11:19,416 --> 00:11:21,250
(Their defense is broken again.)

238
00:11:21,251 --> 00:11:23,119
They lost another point.

239
00:11:23,287 --> 00:11:25,755
Shujitsu High is pushing them hard.

240
00:11:26,023 --> 00:11:30,359
Riona's serves are working
very effectively.

241
00:11:30,736 --> 00:11:33,538
The score goes from 8 to 2 to 8 to 6.

242
00:11:33,563 --> 00:11:34,997
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 6
: Wonder Dogs 8)

243
00:11:34,998 --> 00:11:35,998
It was a good chance.

244
00:11:36,333 --> 00:11:38,734
It's a shame we missed it!

245
00:11:39,403 --> 00:11:43,606
(Their unease spreads rapidly.)

246
00:11:43,607 --> 00:11:46,576
I think that's where it began.

247
00:11:47,577 --> 00:11:49,811
I made the first reception mistake,

248
00:11:50,247 --> 00:11:54,683
and I kept making receiving errors
in a series.

249
00:11:55,152 --> 00:11:57,420
(The momentum shifted to the opponent
in a flash.)

250
00:11:57,421 --> 00:11:59,956
I tried to make it up for it,

251
00:12:00,350 --> 00:12:02,451
but it was really hard
to recover mentally.

252
00:12:04,961 --> 00:12:08,197
(The lead is down to two.)

253
00:12:08,732 --> 00:12:11,167
(Riona's fourth serve in a row!)

254
00:12:11,827 --> 00:12:16,264
(We must stop this serving frenzy.)

255
00:12:19,176 --> 00:12:21,377
Her serve isn't that strong.

256
00:12:21,378 --> 00:12:23,479
It's just that the ball is moving
erratically.

257
00:12:27,818 --> 00:12:29,185
Riona serves again.

258
00:12:32,161 --> 00:12:33,022
Chae Rim.

259
00:12:34,091 --> 00:12:35,658
It's a chance!

260
00:12:35,659 --> 00:12:37,093
(Will it be another receive error?)

261
00:12:40,464 --> 00:12:41,431
(Serve ace again)

262
00:12:41,431 --> 00:12:44,300
With another serve ace,
the score has closed to one!

263
00:12:45,035 --> 00:12:48,838
(Five straight points!)

264
00:12:49,372 --> 00:12:51,406
- Rei!
- Rei!

265
00:12:51,909 --> 00:12:54,743
(With Riona's appearance on the court,)

266
00:12:55,145 --> 00:12:58,414
(the momentum is completely shifted.)

267
00:12:58,415 --> 00:12:59,548
Is her serve hard to receive?

268
00:12:59,950 --> 00:13:02,852
I told you it's just a lot of moving.

269
00:13:03,153 --> 00:13:05,187
With consecutive serve aces,

270
00:13:05,455 --> 00:13:09,024
she gained confidence,
helping her serve even stronger.

271
00:13:09,693 --> 00:13:12,762
With the score of 7 to 8,
the lead is down to 1.

272
00:13:14,264 --> 00:13:15,364
(Peeking)

273
00:13:23,122 --> 00:13:24,706
Slightly over to the right.

274
00:13:24,975 --> 00:13:26,008
(Easy reception)

275
00:13:26,009 --> 00:13:27,143
The players are gathered.

276
00:13:29,012 --> 00:13:30,112
Yes!

277
00:13:30,647 --> 00:13:32,047
Smash to the middle!

278
00:13:32,048 --> 00:13:34,249
(Another defense failure)

279
00:13:34,289 --> 00:13:37,658
I've allowed five points in this spot.
I'm sorry!

280
00:13:40,757 --> 00:13:42,091
Her serve is formidable.

281
00:13:43,093 --> 00:13:44,593
They have to be able to receive it!

282
00:13:45,214 --> 00:13:48,951
Six points went to the same spot
against Wonder Dogs.

283
00:13:49,533 --> 00:13:53,035
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 8
: Wonder Dogs 8)

284
00:13:58,508 --> 00:14:02,144
(Throwing her body to receive it
and maintain the lead)

285
00:14:05,181 --> 00:14:06,548
(Defense failure once again)

286
00:14:06,550 --> 00:14:08,818
Riona serves an ace again!

287
00:14:09,619 --> 00:14:13,055
She's made numerous aces already.
Incredible.

288
00:14:13,056 --> 00:14:15,624
Making a powerful serve is important,

289
00:14:15,625 --> 00:14:20,529
but it's never easy to make
strong serves in a row.

290
00:14:22,999 --> 00:14:23,966
Timeout.

291
00:14:26,136 --> 00:14:29,004
(Wonder Dogs' timeout)

292
00:14:29,005 --> 00:14:31,841
Right now, our receives aren't
working at all.

293
00:14:31,841 --> 00:14:33,709
You were all going under.

294
00:14:33,710 --> 00:14:34,944
- Is their serve strong?
- No.

295
00:14:34,945 --> 00:14:35,978
It's not strong!

296
00:14:35,979 --> 00:14:38,481
It's just that they're precise
with their serve placement.

297
00:14:38,481 --> 00:14:40,282
Let's get our blocking positions right.

298
00:14:40,283 --> 00:14:42,451
- Where should you wait?
- In the middle.

299
00:14:42,452 --> 00:14:44,353
When we block,
if we target the center of the ball,

300
00:14:44,354 --> 00:14:47,189
there's really nowhere for the ball to go.

301
00:14:47,190 --> 00:14:49,958
If you block right in the middle,
they won't have any angles.

302
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:51,494
Make sure to take your positions
on the sides properly.

303
00:14:53,363 --> 00:14:58,167
(Block failed
due to incorrect hand positioning.)

304
00:14:58,277 --> 00:15:01,079
(The key blocking strategy
she's emphasized...)

305
00:15:01,104 --> 00:15:03,339
(since the very beginning of training)

306
00:15:03,475 --> 00:15:06,008
So, what will we be blocking?

307
00:15:06,276 --> 00:15:12,448
(Blocking the gaps)

308
00:15:12,449 --> 00:15:13,616
It could've been blocked.

309
00:15:13,617 --> 00:15:15,117
- Position yourselves on the sides well.
- Okay.

310
00:15:15,118 --> 00:15:17,119
- Let's not concede points anymore.
- We can do it!

311
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,053
In 1, 2, 3!

312
00:15:18,054 --> 00:15:19,688
I'm sorry.

313
00:15:19,689 --> 00:15:20,956
Go further in.

314
00:15:20,957 --> 00:15:23,625
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 9
: Wonder Dogs 8)

315
00:15:23,994 --> 00:15:24,994
The score is 8 to 9.

316
00:15:26,296 --> 00:15:27,630
(Riona's seventh serve)

317
00:15:29,607 --> 00:15:31,538
Let's block just one.

318
00:15:34,927 --> 00:15:35,793
Hey!

319
00:15:35,895 --> 00:15:37,496
It's okay. Hit it!

320
00:15:39,131 --> 00:15:40,164
No!

321
00:15:40,267 --> 00:15:41,833
It wasn't easy, but they saved it.

322
00:15:43,336 --> 00:15:44,202
No!

323
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:47,572
(Block point)

324
00:15:48,741 --> 00:15:50,275
- Sorry.
- The serve is over!

325
00:15:52,111 --> 00:15:56,314
Coach Kim's point about targeting
the center was key.

326
00:15:56,315 --> 00:15:58,082
(Perfectly blocking Shujitsu)

327
00:15:58,651 --> 00:16:00,352
Go!

328
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:03,288
They finally blocked Riona's serve.

329
00:16:05,691 --> 00:16:08,259
(It's about time
they turned the momentum around.)

330
00:16:08,284 --> 00:16:09,694
I have to do something for the team.

331
00:16:10,316 --> 00:16:12,049
However it may be,

332
00:16:12,831 --> 00:16:13,994
I must contribute to the team.

333
00:16:15,167 --> 00:16:17,335
(We'll end the game in this set.)

334
00:16:17,336 --> 00:16:18,403
Again!

335
00:16:18,404 --> 00:16:19,371
(Chae Rim out, Song Hee in)

336
00:16:19,605 --> 00:16:20,838
Focus!

337
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:21,973
Na Yeon.

338
00:16:22,675 --> 00:16:23,575
Give it to Seung Ju.

339
00:16:25,578 --> 00:16:26,945
(Uchida Mimi's serve)

340
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:31,583
Lift it again.

341
00:16:34,186 --> 00:16:35,119
Seung Ju again.

342
00:16:37,532 --> 00:16:39,066
They followed it and dug it up!

343
00:16:39,091 --> 00:16:40,080
(Monstrous defense)

344
00:16:40,927 --> 00:16:41,894
Set it!

345
00:16:41,894 --> 00:16:44,596
(But the ball is set to Seung Ju again.)

346
00:16:45,306 --> 00:16:47,040
The short shot is in!

347
00:16:47,041 --> 00:16:49,276
(Finally, a spike point from Seung Ju)

348
00:16:55,350 --> 00:16:57,017
(Hyeon Jeong's serve)

349
00:17:00,888 --> 00:17:03,857
- It's a serve ace by Hyeon Jeong!
- That's it.

350
00:17:04,592 --> 00:17:06,227
That was a crucial point.

351
00:17:07,128 --> 00:17:08,929
- Let's score one point at a time.
- Okay.

352
00:17:11,966 --> 00:17:15,202
(The momentum has shifted to our side.)

353
00:17:19,774 --> 00:17:20,707
A toss to the right.

354
00:17:20,942 --> 00:17:21,775
Spike.

355
00:17:21,776 --> 00:17:23,343
- That's it!
- Another point!

356
00:17:23,504 --> 00:17:25,205
They scored a point again!

357
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:26,214
(Three points in a row)

358
00:17:28,268 --> 00:17:29,668
That was nice!

359
00:17:31,219 --> 00:17:33,120
This is our chance.

360
00:17:33,421 --> 00:17:36,123
To shift the momentum,
the most effective tools...

361
00:17:36,124 --> 00:17:38,225
- are blocking and serving.
- Yes.

362
00:17:38,919 --> 00:17:42,054
They've just scored using those two.

363
00:17:42,607 --> 00:17:44,308
Now, the key is to maintain this momentum.

364
00:17:44,909 --> 00:17:46,109
(Seung Ju is on a roll.)

365
00:17:46,110 --> 00:17:46,943
Hit it!

366
00:17:48,146 --> 00:17:48,946
Spike.

367
00:17:49,482 --> 00:17:51,149
(Preparing to jump for the chance ball)

368
00:17:51,182 --> 00:17:51,982
Hye In.

369
00:17:52,049 --> 00:17:53,883
She jumps and smashes it!

370
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:56,720
To the right!

371
00:17:57,989 --> 00:18:00,357
(Like a battle
between a spear and a shield)

372
00:18:00,358 --> 00:18:02,259
Check position one first.

373
00:18:03,395 --> 00:18:06,997
- There she goes, Seung Ju!
- That was nice.

374
00:18:07,021 --> 00:18:09,063
One more point.

375
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:10,088
Mine!

376
00:18:11,528 --> 00:18:13,426
Hit it deep, Seung Ju!

377
00:18:14,857 --> 00:18:16,091
(Her deep spike...)

378
00:18:16,116 --> 00:18:17,949
(shakes the tough defense.)

379
00:18:17,949 --> 00:18:20,316
Nice one, Seung Ju!

380
00:18:21,516 --> 00:18:22,582
Pyo Seung Ju.

381
00:18:22,882 --> 00:18:25,016
(The rookie coach's ace up her sleeve)

382
00:18:25,148 --> 00:18:27,881
(She has Pyo Seung Ju in the Wonder Dogs!)

383
00:18:28,882 --> 00:18:29,882
Please!

384
00:18:30,116 --> 00:18:33,182
Back Chae Rim spikes,
and the ball lands inside the court!

385
00:18:33,182 --> 00:18:35,716
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 14
: Wonder Dogs 15)

386
00:18:37,516 --> 00:18:39,682
(With Myoung Hwa's quick attack,)

387
00:18:40,216 --> 00:18:43,282
(Wonder Dogs get their flow back.)

388
00:18:43,949 --> 00:18:46,082
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 15
: Wonder Dogs 16)

389
00:18:46,082 --> 00:18:48,816
It's 16 to 15 with the Wonder Dogs
leading by a point.

390
00:18:48,816 --> 00:18:51,649
And we're now on the fourth set's
second technical timeout.

391
00:19:00,678 --> 00:19:02,912
Set the ball to the right.

392
00:19:02,912 --> 00:19:05,012
- The right side. Got it?
- Yes, Coach.

393
00:19:07,545 --> 00:19:08,745
In 1, 2, 3.

394
00:19:08,745 --> 00:19:10,678
(The Wonder Dogs are leading by a point.)

395
00:19:11,912 --> 00:19:15,445
(They must maintain the gap!)

396
00:19:16,812 --> 00:19:18,478
- Chae Rim, mark number 1.
- Yes.

397
00:19:19,712 --> 00:19:23,378
Check numbers 1 and 16 on the side!

398
00:19:26,512 --> 00:19:27,778
(Marking numbers 1 and 16)

399
00:19:28,545 --> 00:19:30,845
(But number 9 is moving
to the right alone?)

400
00:19:32,612 --> 00:19:34,045
(Tossing to the right as instructed)

401
00:19:34,045 --> 00:19:35,712
She tossed to the right. Spike!

402
00:19:36,245 --> 00:19:37,312
They score with a block out.

403
00:19:37,312 --> 00:19:39,078
(A block out after the ball hits
Chae Rim's forehead)

404
00:19:40,112 --> 00:19:42,445
That's it.

405
00:19:42,687 --> 00:19:44,787
Receive the ball first.

406
00:19:44,812 --> 00:19:46,278
(Immediately allowing a tie)

407
00:19:49,178 --> 00:19:51,112
Receive it! That's fine.

408
00:19:51,112 --> 00:19:52,312
Cover her!

409
00:19:52,412 --> 00:19:53,445
Young In!

410
00:19:54,545 --> 00:19:55,912
Again.

411
00:19:56,245 --> 00:19:57,945
Go slowly. Nice one.

412
00:19:59,945 --> 00:20:01,845
(A long rally due to fierce defense!)

413
00:20:01,845 --> 00:20:03,178
Na Yeon, slowly.

414
00:20:04,945 --> 00:20:05,945
Hit it!

415
00:20:07,012 --> 00:20:09,045
Back Chae Rim hits the antenna.

416
00:20:09,712 --> 00:20:12,745
(The team loses the point on the antenna.)

417
00:20:18,345 --> 00:20:21,312
(They make an unusual error.)

418
00:20:25,412 --> 00:20:26,712
Look at that player.

419
00:20:26,712 --> 00:20:29,378
She's exhausted.

420
00:20:30,712 --> 00:20:33,312
She's run out of energy.

421
00:20:33,312 --> 00:20:34,945
Everyone's tired.

422
00:20:35,212 --> 00:20:37,878
I felt my strength was running out.

423
00:20:39,545 --> 00:20:41,178
(After that,)

424
00:20:42,078 --> 00:20:43,878
(Young In makes a line out error.)

425
00:20:44,845 --> 00:20:47,545
We gradually fell off track.

426
00:20:48,978 --> 00:20:51,412
The Wonder Dogs look quite exhausted.

427
00:20:51,945 --> 00:20:53,812
This is what we've worried about...

428
00:20:53,812 --> 00:20:55,978
in the match with high school students.

429
00:21:00,445 --> 00:21:01,712
Mine. Na Yeon!

430
00:21:05,412 --> 00:21:07,378
(Shujitsu High School students are
still energetic.)

431
00:21:09,578 --> 00:21:11,878
(The Wonder Dogs are struggling
to get a single receive.)

432
00:21:14,012 --> 00:21:15,045
Here it comes.

433
00:21:16,651 --> 00:21:19,217
Set the ball!

434
00:21:19,884 --> 00:21:21,117
Young In, just hit it!

435
00:21:21,584 --> 00:21:23,351
(Even Young In is wobbling.)

436
00:21:24,717 --> 00:21:25,951
(They know there's an attack.)

437
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:26,984
It's coming.

438
00:21:27,617 --> 00:21:29,284
(But their legs won't move easily.)

439
00:21:29,284 --> 00:21:30,351
Spike to the middle!

440
00:21:30,584 --> 00:21:32,717
(They fail to defend in the end.)

441
00:21:33,784 --> 00:21:36,317
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 21
: Wonder Dogs 19)

442
00:21:37,584 --> 00:21:39,984
(Timeout)

443
00:21:40,284 --> 00:21:42,984
(Coach Kim decides to request a timeout.)

444
00:21:43,451 --> 00:21:44,517
Hurry up!

445
00:21:44,684 --> 00:21:45,684
It's okay.

446
00:21:45,684 --> 00:21:48,151
What should you do
when you can't get a point?

447
00:21:48,151 --> 00:21:50,051
You should quickly go
to number 3 for defense.

448
00:21:50,051 --> 00:21:51,117
What are you doing?

449
00:21:51,117 --> 00:21:52,117
Go to number 3.

450
00:21:52,251 --> 00:21:53,951
The rally won't be over right away.

451
00:21:53,951 --> 00:21:55,951
- Move fast to your positions.
- Yes, Coach.

452
00:21:55,951 --> 00:21:57,951
- Let's aim for a side out.
- At least one.

453
00:21:57,951 --> 00:21:59,451
(Let's get the serve back.)

454
00:21:59,451 --> 00:22:00,451
One by one.

455
00:22:01,417 --> 00:22:02,817
Let's stay strong.

456
00:22:03,384 --> 00:22:04,717
I told you before.

457
00:22:04,717 --> 00:22:07,451
The ball only goes straight,
not on high shots.

458
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:09,751
If you keep your positions,
you can defend easily.

459
00:22:09,751 --> 00:22:12,117
- Yes, Coach.
- Keep your spots properly on the side.

460
00:22:12,117 --> 00:22:13,184
- Got it?
- Understood.

461
00:22:13,184 --> 00:22:14,284
Just one!

462
00:22:14,284 --> 00:22:15,517
Toss the ball here.

463
00:22:15,517 --> 00:22:16,684
It's okay.

464
00:22:16,684 --> 00:22:17,917
In 1, 2, 3.

465
00:22:17,917 --> 00:22:19,317
The serve isn't strong, so push it.

466
00:22:19,884 --> 00:22:21,784
Na Yeon, toss it to the back.

467
00:22:21,784 --> 00:22:22,851
You can give it to them.

468
00:22:23,684 --> 00:22:25,751
We just need to earn this point!

469
00:22:26,017 --> 00:22:27,917
Only one, really.

470
00:22:28,284 --> 00:22:29,284
Get ready.

471
00:22:29,284 --> 00:22:31,051
(We must score here.)

472
00:22:32,051 --> 00:22:34,451
(Glancing)

473
00:22:35,451 --> 00:22:36,884
One more time!

474
00:22:37,817 --> 00:22:39,384
One more serve!

475
00:22:43,251 --> 00:22:46,717
(Number 9, Shujitsu High's serve queen,
is back.)

476
00:22:47,644 --> 00:22:49,210
Check where the ball lands
after the serve.

477
00:22:49,997 --> 00:22:52,930
Move your legs! The ball will drop.

478
00:22:56,917 --> 00:22:59,317
(Uchida Riona serves.)

479
00:23:00,317 --> 00:23:01,351
(Nice reception!)

480
00:23:01,351 --> 00:23:02,384
Na Yeon!

481
00:23:03,151 --> 00:23:04,151
Okay.

482
00:23:05,317 --> 00:23:07,084
(She tries a quick attack.)

483
00:23:09,117 --> 00:23:11,051
Here it comes!

484
00:23:11,217 --> 00:23:12,451
(Let's go!)

485
00:23:15,284 --> 00:23:17,084
That's it, Back Chae Rim!

486
00:23:17,084 --> 00:23:18,151
(They score with a block.)

487
00:23:18,151 --> 00:23:20,584
- We're just getting started.
- One more point.

488
00:23:20,951 --> 00:23:23,817
Chae Rim, that's a great spot.

489
00:23:25,084 --> 00:23:29,317
Chae Rim was defending the left side,

490
00:23:29,317 --> 00:23:33,184
but she went all the way
to the middle to block the ball.

491
00:23:33,184 --> 00:23:35,384
Chae Rim must be the most tired one.

492
00:23:35,384 --> 00:23:37,951
She's had the most attacks
throughout the four sets.

493
00:23:37,951 --> 00:23:39,017
You're right.

494
00:23:39,017 --> 00:23:40,051
(Back Chae Rim serves.)

495
00:23:40,417 --> 00:23:41,451
That was a nice serve.

496
00:23:43,184 --> 00:23:44,384
(Spike!)

497
00:23:44,384 --> 00:23:46,017
- That's it.
- They saved the ball.

498
00:23:46,017 --> 00:23:47,517
The team defended well.

499
00:23:47,517 --> 00:23:48,617
(Where will the ball go?)

500
00:23:49,917 --> 00:23:50,951
Pyo Seung Ju!

501
00:23:51,517 --> 00:23:52,551
It's popped up!

502
00:23:55,351 --> 00:23:56,351
It's out!

503
00:23:56,351 --> 00:23:57,684
(Is it out?)

504
00:23:57,817 --> 00:23:59,417
Touch out!

505
00:23:59,717 --> 00:24:01,117
(We didn't touch the ball.)

506
00:24:01,617 --> 00:24:03,051
- It's out!
- All right.

507
00:24:03,551 --> 00:24:04,684
It's 21 to 21.

508
00:24:04,684 --> 00:24:05,684
Great job.

509
00:24:05,684 --> 00:24:07,284
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 21
: Wonder Dogs 21)

510
00:24:07,584 --> 00:24:10,017
(This is so intense.)

511
00:24:10,017 --> 00:24:12,351
- The score is finally tied.
- It's a tie.

512
00:24:12,351 --> 00:24:15,084
(Shujitsu High School allows
the score to be tied.)

513
00:24:15,084 --> 00:24:17,584
There's not a single easy point
in this set.

514
00:24:17,684 --> 00:24:19,551
Focus on your target player.

515
00:24:19,717 --> 00:24:21,684
Eyes on number 3 first.

516
00:24:21,917 --> 00:24:22,951
Check number 3!

517
00:24:23,784 --> 00:24:26,417
(They aim for number 3
of Shujitsu High School while blocking.)

518
00:24:28,584 --> 00:24:29,584
(Give it to me!)

519
00:24:30,917 --> 00:24:32,551
(Number 3 jumps.)

520
00:24:32,851 --> 00:24:34,817
(We'll block it...)

521
00:24:34,817 --> 00:24:36,851
(no matter what.)

522
00:24:36,851 --> 00:24:38,684
They blocked it in the middle!

523
00:24:40,151 --> 00:24:41,151
She dumped the ball.

524
00:24:42,084 --> 00:24:43,917
(Blocking number 3 again!)

525
00:24:44,417 --> 00:24:45,417
Take it easy.

526
00:24:46,617 --> 00:24:48,317
(They blocked number 3 once more!)

527
00:24:48,517 --> 00:24:49,617
Set the ball to me.

528
00:24:50,184 --> 00:24:51,417
- Seung Ju!
- Kim Hyeon Jeong.

529
00:24:53,817 --> 00:24:54,817
(A powerful spike)

530
00:24:54,817 --> 00:24:56,717
- It's a standing jump spike!
- Nice attack!

531
00:24:57,384 --> 00:24:58,751
What a merciless attack!

532
00:24:59,384 --> 00:25:01,251
- Let's go.
- The players know...

533
00:25:01,251 --> 00:25:04,251
that they've got a few points left.

534
00:25:04,251 --> 00:25:06,151
Pyo Seung Ju is aware of it.

535
00:25:08,951 --> 00:25:10,717
Pyo Seung Ju!

536
00:25:11,551 --> 00:25:13,751
She's so awesome.

537
00:25:14,184 --> 00:25:15,684
Seung Ju!

538
00:25:16,984 --> 00:25:18,784
They may be really tired right now,

539
00:25:18,784 --> 00:25:21,584
but it would be tough to handle
when they lose this set.

540
00:25:21,584 --> 00:25:22,684
One more point.

541
00:25:24,717 --> 00:25:26,317
If we lose more games,

542
00:25:26,317 --> 00:25:29,284
all our hard work will be for nothing.

543
00:25:29,284 --> 00:25:30,617
(To keep the Wonder Dogs together,)

544
00:25:30,617 --> 00:25:34,751
I have to get the next point for us
to have a chance.

545
00:25:34,751 --> 00:25:35,751
(I must pull this off.)

546
00:25:38,351 --> 00:25:40,217
(The game continues.)

547
00:25:42,617 --> 00:25:43,617
Pyo Seung Ju!

548
00:25:48,151 --> 00:25:49,384
They score!

549
00:25:49,384 --> 00:25:50,417
Great.

550
00:25:52,017 --> 00:25:54,084
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 22
: Wonder Dogs 23)

551
00:25:54,084 --> 00:25:55,084
One more point.

552
00:25:55,084 --> 00:25:58,751
Pyo Seung Ju is squeezing
out every last bit she has left.

553
00:25:58,751 --> 00:26:00,884
(She can't let go of her responsibility
as the captain.)

554
00:26:02,051 --> 00:26:04,817
It's 23 to 22, and the Wonder Dogs are
leading by a point.

555
00:26:04,817 --> 00:26:05,851
(Two points left to win)

556
00:26:08,451 --> 00:26:10,517
(They received it well.)

557
00:26:11,851 --> 00:26:13,251
A back toss. Spike.

558
00:26:13,251 --> 00:26:14,784
(Please!)

559
00:26:14,784 --> 00:26:16,251
One more. Please!

560
00:26:18,451 --> 00:26:19,884
A block touch out.

561
00:26:21,917 --> 00:26:24,051
Yeah! Nice!

562
00:26:24,251 --> 00:26:28,817
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 23
: Wonder Dogs 23)

563
00:26:29,751 --> 00:26:31,284
(Shujitsu High School ties
the game again.)

564
00:26:31,284 --> 00:26:34,017
- They must score first for a set point.
- That's right.

565
00:26:34,042 --> 00:26:36,409
(The Wonder Dogs need this set point.)

566
00:26:39,851 --> 00:26:41,117
Side out!

567
00:26:41,117 --> 00:26:43,617
(It's okay! Let's get the serve back!)

568
00:26:43,642 --> 00:26:46,476
They only need to get the set point
to relieve their pressure.

569
00:26:48,517 --> 00:26:50,384
- Okay.
- That's it. Do it calmly.

570
00:26:52,084 --> 00:26:53,151
Spike.

571
00:26:53,151 --> 00:26:54,584
(She spikes with desperation!)

572
00:26:58,151 --> 00:27:00,217
It's out.

573
00:27:01,584 --> 00:27:02,584
She's exhausted.

574
00:27:15,451 --> 00:27:16,884
It's okay.

575
00:27:18,384 --> 00:27:21,151
Let's do it again. Cover each other!

576
00:27:22,817 --> 00:27:23,851
Slow down.

577
00:27:23,851 --> 00:27:26,251
(More haste, less speed.)

578
00:27:28,184 --> 00:27:30,984
(We must hold it together,
no matter what.)

579
00:27:32,084 --> 00:27:34,684
Set point for Shujitsu High School
in the fourth set.

580
00:27:35,584 --> 00:27:37,784
(Ishida Megumi, the ace
of the team, serves.)

581
00:27:37,784 --> 00:27:39,317
Mine. Way to go!

582
00:27:39,317 --> 00:27:40,484
(She smoothly receives the ball...)

583
00:27:40,484 --> 00:27:41,584
(and passes to Seung Ju!)

584
00:27:42,817 --> 00:27:44,117
(Dropping down in exhaustion)

585
00:27:44,951 --> 00:27:45,984
They defended it.

586
00:27:45,984 --> 00:27:48,084
(Tossing to Seung Ju's side)

587
00:27:48,384 --> 00:27:50,151
(Standing up)

588
00:27:51,451 --> 00:27:52,484
Spike!

589
00:27:52,484 --> 00:27:53,951
(I'll block it at all costs.)

590
00:27:55,117 --> 00:27:56,584
(They missed it.)

591
00:27:57,084 --> 00:27:59,517
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High School 25
: Wonder Dogs 23)

592
00:28:02,551 --> 00:28:03,651
(We won!)

593
00:28:03,651 --> 00:28:06,050
With the score of 23 to 25,

594
00:28:06,051 --> 00:28:06,918
Good. Thank you.

595
00:28:06,918 --> 00:28:08,986
Shujitsu High School wins the fourth set.

596
00:28:08,987 --> 00:28:13,357
(Shujitsu High School ends up winning
the fourth set after a fierce match.)

597
00:28:17,729 --> 00:28:22,132
It's the first five-set game
for Wonder Dogs.

598
00:28:22,133 --> 00:28:24,001
(Shujitsu High School 0 : Wonder Dogs 1)

599
00:28:24,002 --> 00:28:25,970
Although Wonder Dogs took the first set,

600
00:28:25,971 --> 00:28:29,640
losing the third and fourth
has pushed the game to a fifth.

601
00:28:29,641 --> 00:28:30,674
(Shujitsu High School 2 : Wonder Dogs 2)

602
00:28:30,942 --> 00:28:33,710
(They prolong the match to the fifth set.)

603
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:34,845
It's driving me crazy.

604
00:28:41,653 --> 00:28:44,788
Since they've never gone
to a fifth set before,

605
00:28:44,789 --> 00:28:46,390
they must be exhausted...

606
00:28:46,391 --> 00:28:49,059
now that the fourth has just ended.

607
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:50,127
That's right.

608
00:28:50,128 --> 00:28:53,564
(Behind the exhausted
Wonder Dogs players,)

609
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:57,235
(Coach Kim falls silent.)

610
00:28:58,303 --> 00:28:59,870
There were players...

611
00:28:59,938 --> 00:29:02,840
who were completely drained.

612
00:29:03,742 --> 00:29:06,944
I kept thinking hard
about what I could do...

613
00:29:07,112 --> 00:29:08,512
from the bench.

614
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:10,114
All I could do was trust my players.

615
00:29:12,784 --> 00:29:14,118
Let's get ahead early in the set.

616
00:29:14,119 --> 00:29:15,286
- It's okay. We can do this!
- Okay!

617
00:29:15,287 --> 00:29:16,854
Let's shout it out
and give everything we've got.

618
00:29:16,855 --> 00:29:18,422
- Let's go!
- Let's do this!

619
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:20,090
How many points were we
behind when we lost?

620
00:29:20,091 --> 00:29:21,625
- Two points.
- Just two!

621
00:29:21,626 --> 00:29:24,795
Think about it.
How many mistakes did we make?

622
00:29:25,931 --> 00:29:28,032
Seung Ju, when the ball doesn't
come right, just pass to the center.

623
00:29:28,033 --> 00:29:29,267
Why did you go that way?

624
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:31,902
- You can just pass to the center.
- Sorry.

625
00:29:32,103 --> 00:29:34,137
- And you need to set more.
- Okay.

626
00:29:34,139 --> 00:29:35,373
Don't worry about precision too much.

627
00:29:35,373 --> 00:29:37,174
Just focus on the basics.

628
00:29:37,709 --> 00:29:39,043
We've come this far.

629
00:29:39,044 --> 00:29:40,711
We've done enough.

630
00:29:40,979 --> 00:29:43,180
Let's leave no regrets.

631
00:29:43,181 --> 00:29:45,149
No, it's not about no regrets.
We must win.

632
00:29:46,585 --> 00:29:49,086
At this point, when they're reaching
their physical limits,

633
00:29:49,321 --> 00:29:51,822
I hope the players remember
why they came back...

634
00:29:51,823 --> 00:29:54,024
to play volleyball
in the Wonder Dogs uniform.

635
00:29:54,025 --> 00:29:56,960
- I really want them to ask themselves.
- That's right.

636
00:29:57,162 --> 00:29:58,996
- Just focus on our game.
- Okay.

637
00:29:58,997 --> 00:30:00,598
- In 1, 2, 3!
- Let's go!

638
00:30:00,598 --> 00:30:03,533
- Remember the basics!
- Let's go!

639
00:30:03,535 --> 00:30:04,502
The basics!

640
00:30:05,704 --> 00:30:08,572
The start of this set is crucial!

641
00:30:09,140 --> 00:30:11,341
(The final set to decide their fate)

642
00:30:11,509 --> 00:30:13,543
(To win...)

643
00:30:13,770 --> 00:30:15,270
(or to be defeated)

644
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:18,148
(There's no turning back.)

645
00:30:18,149 --> 00:30:20,717
The last set goes to 15 points,

646
00:30:20,719 --> 00:30:22,219
- not 25.
- Yes, 15 points.

647
00:30:23,321 --> 00:30:25,922
That means they can't afford
to give away early points.

648
00:30:26,791 --> 00:30:29,626
The final set begins now!

649
00:30:33,031 --> 00:30:33,964
Here!

650
00:30:34,933 --> 00:30:36,467
(Screaming)

651
00:30:38,069 --> 00:30:39,036
(A reception error)

652
00:30:39,037 --> 00:30:41,171
Wonder Dogs lose a point on an error.

653
00:30:41,639 --> 00:30:43,740
(Shujitsu takes the early lead.)

654
00:30:43,742 --> 00:30:45,242
Nice!

655
00:30:48,346 --> 00:30:50,981
Chae Rim needs to calm down
and stay composed.

656
00:30:51,116 --> 00:30:53,384
Chae Rim, their serves tend
to drop suddenly.

657
00:31:00,258 --> 00:31:01,258
- Here!
- Hey!

658
00:31:01,259 --> 00:31:02,426
Chae Rim receives it cleanly.

659
00:31:03,929 --> 00:31:04,996
(Groaning)

660
00:31:05,463 --> 00:31:07,431
Seung Ju's fierce spike.

661
00:31:07,432 --> 00:31:09,800
(A piercing spike by Seung Ju)

662
00:31:11,403 --> 00:31:12,303
Nice! That's it!

663
00:31:12,604 --> 00:31:14,071
Forget the mistake!

664
00:31:14,572 --> 00:31:16,306
All that matters is scoring.

665
00:31:19,844 --> 00:31:23,246
(Seung Ju's serve)

666
00:31:23,248 --> 00:31:24,782
Myoung Hwa, keep your eyes on number one.

667
00:31:25,350 --> 00:31:26,417
- Number one!
- Number one!

668
00:31:26,418 --> 00:31:27,451
(Mark number one!)

669
00:31:28,053 --> 00:31:29,120
Number one!

670
00:31:31,923 --> 00:31:33,590
Here she comes!

671
00:31:34,092 --> 00:31:37,494
(Number one jumps up,
just as Yeon Koung predicted.)

672
00:31:37,495 --> 00:31:39,162
Myoung Hwa, eyes on number one!

673
00:31:44,328 --> 00:31:45,361
That's it!

674
00:31:45,804 --> 00:31:47,138
A point by Myoung Hwa!

675
00:31:47,138 --> 00:31:49,139
Myoung Hwa's precise block earns a point.

676
00:31:49,307 --> 00:31:52,442
(We've got the momentum!)

677
00:31:53,144 --> 00:31:54,478
Let's go!

678
00:31:58,445 --> 00:31:59,650
The score is 1 to 2.

679
00:32:01,486 --> 00:32:02,252
Here!

680
00:32:02,253 --> 00:32:03,353
(The Wonder Dogs are on a roll.)

681
00:32:04,022 --> 00:32:05,990
(Peeking)

682
00:32:07,025 --> 00:32:07,691
(Screaming)

683
00:32:09,327 --> 00:32:10,527
A quick attack point by Myoung Hwa!

684
00:32:10,528 --> 00:32:11,661
(The Wonder Dogs' quick attack point)

685
00:32:12,197 --> 00:32:13,731
(Smiling)

686
00:32:14,032 --> 00:32:15,866
Let's go!

687
00:32:18,069 --> 00:32:19,503
The Wonder Dogs are on a roll!

688
00:32:19,504 --> 00:32:22,840
Next serve, Myoung Hwa.

689
00:32:27,079 --> 00:32:27,978
Serve by Myoung Hwa.

690
00:32:30,014 --> 00:32:30,914
(Swaying)

691
00:32:31,850 --> 00:32:33,184
Ishida is off-balance!

692
00:32:35,153 --> 00:32:36,220
(A forced tip?)

693
00:32:36,221 --> 00:32:37,121
Here it comes.

694
00:32:37,355 --> 00:32:38,221
That's it!

695
00:32:38,223 --> 00:32:39,490
(It's our chance!)

696
00:32:43,528 --> 00:32:44,361
Hey!

697
00:32:44,896 --> 00:32:47,297
Why couldn't she get that?

698
00:32:49,734 --> 00:32:52,035
I've used up all my energy.

699
00:32:52,036 --> 00:32:54,804
That's why I lost focus.

700
00:32:55,382 --> 00:32:57,450
It felt like all the invisible mistakes...

701
00:32:57,475 --> 00:33:00,110
were piling up.

702
00:33:00,311 --> 00:33:01,178
(Starting from Myoung Hwa's error...)
To the right side.

703
00:33:03,648 --> 00:33:04,514
A spike.

704
00:33:04,883 --> 00:33:05,916
No!

705
00:33:06,317 --> 00:33:08,151
Hyeon Jeong, you saw that!

706
00:33:08,153 --> 00:33:09,787
You should've followed it to the right!

707
00:33:13,725 --> 00:33:14,958
A spike to the right side.

708
00:33:14,959 --> 00:33:15,992
(Another mistake)

709
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:17,795
We need to finish this.

710
00:33:20,031 --> 00:33:20,931
Tip.

711
00:33:21,966 --> 00:33:23,600
(A dig error by the libero)

712
00:33:23,768 --> 00:33:24,901
Another point lost.

713
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:26,637
What are you doing?
Why aren't you defending?

714
00:33:26,638 --> 00:33:27,771
(The momentum shifts in an instant.)

715
00:33:27,906 --> 00:33:28,739
To the left.

716
00:33:29,174 --> 00:33:30,040
Another point lost.

717
00:33:30,041 --> 00:33:32,009
I told you to step in closer!

718
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:33,711
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High School 8
: Wonder Dogs 6)

719
00:33:34,379 --> 00:33:37,881
(Technical timeout)

720
00:33:37,916 --> 00:33:39,250
Didn't I tell you to focus on Number Six?

721
00:33:39,717 --> 00:33:41,985
Why'd you go that way?
You should've gone this way.

722
00:33:42,454 --> 00:33:44,121
- I told you not to miss that.
- Okay.

723
00:33:44,122 --> 00:33:46,557
- I told you!
- We need to do this, guys!

724
00:33:46,558 --> 00:33:48,859
Can't you see the setters when blocking?

725
00:33:49,260 --> 00:33:51,027
They fake then send it
to the back. You need to follow that!

726
00:33:51,029 --> 00:33:52,396
- Why aren't you? You have to!
- Okay.

727
00:33:52,397 --> 00:33:53,230
Yes, Coach.

728
00:33:53,231 --> 00:33:54,965
I told you not to swing
your arms like this.

729
00:33:55,333 --> 00:33:56,400
You need to keep them straight.

730
00:33:56,401 --> 00:33:57,801
The defenders will be there.

731
00:33:57,802 --> 00:33:58,969
- Got it?
- Yes.

732
00:33:59,571 --> 00:34:01,972
(But due to fatigue,)

733
00:34:02,707 --> 00:34:05,943
(their morale is visibly low.)

734
00:34:08,113 --> 00:34:09,847
Guys, it's now or never.

735
00:34:09,847 --> 00:34:11,548
- Let's do this.
- We need to try.

736
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:12,549
- Okay.
- Okay.

737
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:15,252
- Let's not give up!
- Now is the time!

738
00:34:15,420 --> 00:34:17,354
Let's do this!

739
00:34:17,355 --> 00:34:18,589
- In 1, 2, 3!
- Let's go!

740
00:34:18,590 --> 00:34:19,690
We've got this!

741
00:34:20,625 --> 00:34:22,326
(Peeking)

742
00:34:24,963 --> 00:34:28,065
Watch Number 19's cross in the middle.

743
00:34:28,466 --> 00:34:31,635
(She orders tight marking on Seung Ju.)

744
00:34:34,639 --> 00:34:37,074
Let's get our rhythm back
and bring our energy up!

745
00:34:39,377 --> 00:34:41,411
There's no time to think
about what we can't do.

746
00:34:41,412 --> 00:34:42,579
We just have to do it.

747
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:44,247
Don't give up, guys!

748
00:34:44,716 --> 00:34:45,783
Watch out!

749
00:34:46,417 --> 00:34:48,419
(They desperately need
to turn the tables.)

750
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:49,753
We need to turn this around here.

751
00:34:49,988 --> 00:34:52,022
Let's make our move now!

752
00:34:52,991 --> 00:34:56,760
(Which team will take the lead
in the second half of the fifth set?)

753
00:34:56,861 --> 00:34:59,329
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High School 9
: Wonder Dogs 6)

754
00:35:01,065 --> 00:35:01,898
My ball!

755
00:35:02,333 --> 00:35:03,166
Seung Ju.

756
00:35:03,635 --> 00:35:04,468
Na Yeon.

757
00:35:05,003 --> 00:35:05,769
Seung Ju.

758
00:35:08,706 --> 00:35:09,572
(Pass dink)

759
00:35:12,377 --> 00:35:13,811
The ball crosses over.

760
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:15,045
Seung Ju.

761
00:35:15,914 --> 00:35:19,216
(A tip by Chae Rim)

762
00:35:20,885 --> 00:35:21,718
(It's a chance!)

763
00:35:21,719 --> 00:35:23,019
That's it!

764
00:35:24,622 --> 00:35:25,855
Spike!

765
00:35:31,763 --> 00:35:32,629
Nice!
(The Wonder Dogs finally score again.)

766
00:35:33,531 --> 00:35:34,531
Please.

767
00:35:34,532 --> 00:35:35,932
Guys, please don't give up.

768
00:35:35,933 --> 00:35:38,268
- Well done!
- Great job.

769
00:35:39,204 --> 00:35:40,171
What's going on?

770
00:35:40,171 --> 00:35:41,538
(But...)

771
00:35:42,373 --> 00:35:43,340
What's going on?

772
00:35:44,876 --> 00:35:48,445
I can't help but notice Seung Ju...

773
00:35:48,446 --> 00:35:50,747
is completely exhausted.

774
00:35:51,182 --> 00:35:54,618
- She can't even jump properly.
- Yes, it's clear.

775
00:35:54,719 --> 00:35:56,553
She's giving everything she's got,

776
00:35:56,688 --> 00:35:59,623
but she's lost the rhythm
she had earlier in the game.

777
00:35:59,624 --> 00:36:00,457
That's right.

778
00:36:02,060 --> 00:36:03,427
It's okay. Take it slow.

779
00:36:03,962 --> 00:36:06,797
Take it slow! Take your time.

780
00:36:08,266 --> 00:36:11,802
Seung Ju, if you can't,
just dink to the center.

781
00:36:13,438 --> 00:36:14,872
(The captain pulls herself together.)

782
00:36:14,872 --> 00:36:16,339
We need this point now.

783
00:36:16,341 --> 00:36:18,075
If we don't catch up here,
we won't get another chance.

784
00:36:19,077 --> 00:36:22,513
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High School 10
: Wonder Dogs 7)

785
00:36:24,349 --> 00:36:25,182
My ball!

786
00:36:25,183 --> 00:36:27,084
(Chae Rim's reception)

787
00:36:29,354 --> 00:36:30,254
(Another attack by Seung Ju)

788
00:36:31,422 --> 00:36:32,989
(It's blocked!)

789
00:36:34,626 --> 00:36:35,793
Go, Chae Rim!

790
00:36:38,529 --> 00:36:39,696
(She runs forward and digs it!)

791
00:36:39,697 --> 00:36:40,597
Great defense!

792
00:36:40,832 --> 00:36:41,698
She jumps and sets!

793
00:36:41,699 --> 00:36:42,766
(A straight-line hit!)

794
00:36:43,835 --> 00:36:44,701
A straight spike!
(It's blocked again!)

795
00:36:46,537 --> 00:36:47,370
Okay!

796
00:36:49,907 --> 00:36:51,741
(Point for the Wonder Dogs?)

797
00:36:52,377 --> 00:36:54,612
(A double contact by Shujitsu High School)

798
00:36:55,713 --> 00:36:59,816
(A violation in which a player
touches the ball twice in succession)

799
00:37:00,184 --> 00:37:01,050
Okay!

800
00:37:02,920 --> 00:37:03,720
Nice!

801
00:37:06,624 --> 00:37:07,891
Luck is on our side! Please!

802
00:37:08,126 --> 00:37:10,194
This score is still...

803
00:37:10,194 --> 00:37:11,561
- within reach.
- Of course, it is.

804
00:37:11,562 --> 00:37:12,762
And the atmosphere...

805
00:37:12,764 --> 00:37:15,733
- isn't on Shujitsu's side either.
- Exactly.

806
00:37:15,733 --> 00:37:18,602
Watch out for the front block!

807
00:37:18,603 --> 00:37:21,238
Myoung Hwa, stay tight on Chae Rim's side.

808
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:23,740
(Watch out for the block
on Chae Rim's side.)

809
00:37:31,316 --> 00:37:32,182
A block!

810
00:37:32,183 --> 00:37:34,284
(A block point...)

811
00:37:34,285 --> 00:37:36,319
(by Chae Rim)

812
00:37:36,621 --> 00:37:38,388
Hey, well done.

813
00:37:39,057 --> 00:37:41,892
(A play that could turn the tables!)

814
00:37:41,893 --> 00:37:42,693
Nice, Chae Rim!

815
00:37:44,095 --> 00:37:45,862
(Here comes the dopamine rush!)

816
00:37:47,565 --> 00:37:48,732
A perfect block!

817
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:51,000
Don't give up until the end!

818
00:37:51,002 --> 00:37:52,703
Keep it going till the end!

819
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:55,872
(Just one point away from catching up!)

820
00:37:55,873 --> 00:37:57,942
Myoung Hwa, it's higher here,

821
00:37:57,943 --> 00:37:59,709
so take half a step closer to Chae Rim.

822
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:03,747
This isn't good.

823
00:38:03,748 --> 00:38:05,748
(The server is...)

824
00:38:05,748 --> 00:38:08,049
Come on, guys! We're almost caught up!

825
00:38:09,652 --> 00:38:12,621
(The ace, team captain Seung Ju's serve)

826
00:38:12,788 --> 00:38:15,523
We really can't afford
a serve error at this point.

827
00:38:15,693 --> 00:38:16,858
- Come on!
- Please.

828
00:38:16,859 --> 00:38:18,927
Come on. You've got a mean swing!

829
00:38:22,631 --> 00:38:26,400
(She scored with serve aces twice today.)

830
00:38:27,136 --> 00:38:31,473
(Captain Pyo's serve is
as good as Myung Hwa's.)

831
00:38:44,543 --> 00:38:45,343
No!

832
00:38:50,082 --> 00:38:51,883
It's okay. We can try again.

833
00:38:54,946 --> 00:38:59,156
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High School 11
: Wonder Dogs 9)

834
00:38:59,984 --> 00:39:04,020
(The momentum is shifting again.)

835
00:39:09,794 --> 00:39:10,693
No matter what happens,

836
00:39:10,928 --> 00:39:15,031
I believe I should always
stay composed on the court.

837
00:39:15,632 --> 00:39:17,301
But I was shaken.

838
00:39:17,501 --> 00:39:20,636
And it was really hard to regain my focus.

839
00:39:20,638 --> 00:39:23,507
Guys, stay strong. We just need one point.

840
00:39:23,875 --> 00:39:24,875
Go again!

841
00:39:25,777 --> 00:39:29,646
(The captain kept driving the team
and leading them forward.)

842
00:39:30,715 --> 00:39:32,816
(But...)

843
00:39:34,652 --> 00:39:35,919
I had no energy left.

844
00:39:38,322 --> 00:39:41,991
Honestly, I only thought,
"What am I going to do now?"

845
00:39:45,329 --> 00:39:46,596
One, two, three!

846
00:39:46,597 --> 00:39:49,566
- Hit it hard!
- You can do this!

847
00:39:49,734 --> 00:39:51,168
Come on, Seung Ju!

848
00:39:51,402 --> 00:39:52,268
Get ready.

849
00:39:55,773 --> 00:39:57,540
(That's right.)

850
00:39:57,541 --> 00:40:01,077
(We're a team.)

851
00:40:01,179 --> 00:40:03,046
(We have a top-class player as coach,)

852
00:40:03,047 --> 00:40:05,416
(coaching staff with their voices
completely hoarse,)

853
00:40:05,716 --> 00:40:08,218
(and strong teammates by our side.)

854
00:40:08,686 --> 00:40:10,487
We're all in this together.

855
00:40:11,155 --> 00:40:12,956
We can trust each other.

856
00:40:13,558 --> 00:40:15,292
The six of us on the court...

857
00:40:15,760 --> 00:40:17,427
promised to do our parts today.

858
00:40:17,428 --> 00:40:18,561
(Trust the teamwork of the players)

859
00:40:25,343 --> 00:40:26,410
Okay! My ball!

860
00:40:28,046 --> 00:40:29,113
- Na Yeon.
- Please!

861
00:40:29,114 --> 00:40:31,482
(Chae Rim...)

862
00:40:31,483 --> 00:40:33,918
(Come on, please!)

863
00:40:36,121 --> 00:40:38,055
- Spike and score!
- Yes!

864
00:40:38,056 --> 00:40:39,723
- It's ten to eleven.
- Sorry about the serve.

865
00:40:39,724 --> 00:40:40,958
No, it's okay.

866
00:40:41,159 --> 00:40:43,627
(Chae Rim covers Seung Ju's miss)

867
00:40:43,628 --> 00:40:46,396
- We have a great chance to catch up.
- We do.

868
00:40:46,531 --> 00:40:47,831
- Let's send in Song Hee.
- Song Hee?

869
00:40:47,866 --> 00:40:49,033
Song Hee!

870
00:40:49,134 --> 00:40:50,034
Song Hee!

871
00:40:50,802 --> 00:40:52,402
Go get them, Song Hee!

872
00:40:52,537 --> 00:40:54,938
All right, they're sending in Song Hee.

873
00:40:55,040 --> 00:40:58,876
- Probably to bring up the defense.
- Yes, after bringing up the serve.

874
00:40:59,411 --> 00:41:02,012
Get to the other side
of the court right away.

875
00:41:02,081 --> 00:41:02,947
Think first.

876
00:41:02,947 --> 00:41:04,381
- That's where they hit. Okay?
- Okay.

877
00:41:05,183 --> 00:41:06,083
Opposite side.

878
00:41:10,642 --> 00:41:13,344
(Serves)

879
00:41:13,746 --> 00:41:15,413
(And moving to the other side
of the court)

880
00:41:17,416 --> 00:41:18,249
Spike!

881
00:41:18,617 --> 00:41:20,418
(The opposite side...)

882
00:41:20,419 --> 00:41:21,819
(is blocked!)

883
00:41:22,288 --> 00:41:23,054
Yes!

884
00:41:24,023 --> 00:41:25,123
They set it!

885
00:41:25,124 --> 00:41:25,957
Please!

886
00:41:25,958 --> 00:41:27,559
(But the defense is shaky.)

887
00:41:29,595 --> 00:41:31,629
(Follow-up spike by Miharu)

888
00:41:32,464 --> 00:41:34,265
It drops inside the court.

889
00:41:34,366 --> 00:41:36,634
(Frustrated)

890
00:41:37,036 --> 00:41:37,869
Hey!

891
00:41:39,805 --> 00:41:41,906
- She is an ace.
- That was a smart play.

892
00:41:41,907 --> 00:41:43,207
It was.

893
00:41:43,475 --> 00:41:45,643
She went deep to take the pace off.

894
00:41:45,644 --> 00:41:46,711
(To Seung Ju, who's out of energy)

895
00:41:47,646 --> 00:41:49,513
Na Yeon! Set it quick.

896
00:41:49,515 --> 00:41:51,182
(Toss to Young In!)

897
00:41:51,650 --> 00:41:54,252
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High School 13
: Wonder Dogs 10)

898
00:41:56,188 --> 00:41:57,021
My ball!

899
00:41:57,022 --> 00:41:58,589
(Aiming for Seung Ju again)

900
00:41:58,924 --> 00:41:59,690
My ball!

901
00:41:59,691 --> 00:42:01,258
(Chae Rim dives and saves it.)

902
00:42:01,794 --> 00:42:02,727
We have to get this one!

903
00:42:02,728 --> 00:42:04,162
(Passes to Young In as discussed)

904
00:42:04,663 --> 00:42:06,197
- Young In, hit it!
- Come on, Young In!

905
00:42:06,198 --> 00:42:08,399
Young In, just this one. Please!

906
00:42:13,105 --> 00:42:15,139
(Direct kill)

907
00:42:15,908 --> 00:42:16,941
That's it!

908
00:42:16,942 --> 00:42:20,378
(Young In did it this time!)

909
00:42:21,046 --> 00:42:23,014
(For their exhausted captain,)

910
00:42:23,515 --> 00:42:27,051
(the teammates throw themselves in.)

911
00:42:27,987 --> 00:42:28,887
I was grateful.

912
00:42:29,555 --> 00:42:32,190
I felt like we were holding each other up.

913
00:42:33,459 --> 00:42:35,693
As long as we don't give up until the end,

914
00:42:36,729 --> 00:42:37,796
we can win this.

915
00:42:39,365 --> 00:42:40,498
Good job.

916
00:42:40,499 --> 00:42:43,267
(It's 13 to 11,
only a two-point difference.)

917
00:42:43,362 --> 00:42:45,096
- The game isn't over yet.
- Of course.

918
00:42:45,104 --> 00:42:47,205
There's absolutely
no reason for them to give up.

919
00:42:47,206 --> 00:42:48,640
Coach, we have Sol.

920
00:42:48,874 --> 00:42:49,640
We can use Sol.

921
00:42:49,641 --> 00:42:52,109
(Go with the substitution!)

922
00:42:52,244 --> 00:42:54,979
- It's 11 to 13.
- They're sending in Sol...

923
00:42:54,980 --> 00:42:57,048
- to raise the block height.
- Yes.

924
00:42:58,517 --> 00:43:00,084
(They are in the lead now,)

925
00:43:00,786 --> 00:43:03,388
(but they still feel nervous.)

926
00:43:04,223 --> 00:43:05,490
Mark player number three.

927
00:43:05,491 --> 00:43:07,058
Sol. Keep an eye.

928
00:43:07,493 --> 00:43:09,160
Hyeon Jeong, they cross a lot.

929
00:43:09,161 --> 00:43:10,895
Watch there first,
but also watch the cross.

930
00:43:11,363 --> 00:43:14,532
You have to watch numbers three and nine!
Numbers three and nine!

931
00:43:14,533 --> 00:43:16,434
Chae Rim, watch number nine!

932
00:43:16,668 --> 00:43:18,268
Go, Sol!

933
00:43:18,270 --> 00:43:20,505
(The Wonder Dogs,
united by their desire to win)

934
00:43:20,806 --> 00:43:22,874
There's definitely a chance.

935
00:43:23,609 --> 00:43:26,044
(Young In's serve)

936
00:43:29,481 --> 00:43:30,548
Okay, okay.

937
00:43:33,052 --> 00:43:34,686
Number three up front!

938
00:43:34,686 --> 00:43:35,819
(As expected, number three attacks.)

939
00:43:39,525 --> 00:43:41,826
It's out! That's out!

940
00:43:41,827 --> 00:43:42,760
We didn't touch it!

941
00:43:42,928 --> 00:43:43,828
Out!

942
00:43:44,830 --> 00:43:47,432
(What is the call?)

943
00:43:49,768 --> 00:43:51,836
(Point to Shujitsu High School!)

944
00:43:51,837 --> 00:43:52,970
Nice!

945
00:43:56,275 --> 00:43:58,309
(The ball didn't hit the blockers,)

946
00:43:58,944 --> 00:44:01,012
(but bounced off the net...)

947
00:44:01,013 --> 00:44:02,914
(and landed inside the court.)

948
00:44:04,750 --> 00:44:09,487
(Shujitsu High's lucky point)

949
00:44:09,488 --> 00:44:11,489
Now, it's 11 to 14.

950
00:44:11,723 --> 00:44:14,358
It's match point for Shujitsu High.

951
00:44:15,227 --> 00:44:17,862
No!

952
00:44:19,331 --> 00:44:24,468
(Everyone is already at their limit.)

953
00:44:25,637 --> 00:44:27,071
I was really desperate.

954
00:44:28,006 --> 00:44:30,374
If we lose again, we're disbanding.

955
00:44:31,710 --> 00:44:35,613
(They already tasted
the bitterness of defeat once.)

956
00:44:36,281 --> 00:44:38,315
Once this moment passes,
the players will be...

957
00:44:38,317 --> 00:44:40,752
left with not just the result,
but the emotions as well.

958
00:44:40,752 --> 00:44:41,785
I hope those emotions...

959
00:44:41,787 --> 00:44:44,289
- are not all regret and disappointment.
- You're right.

960
00:44:46,058 --> 00:44:48,159
(It's too early to give up yet.)

961
00:44:49,161 --> 00:44:52,830
(Sending Na Yeon back in again)

962
00:44:55,033 --> 00:44:58,035
(But the next serve is by...)

963
00:44:59,171 --> 00:45:03,241
(number nine, the serve queen, Riona.)

964
00:45:03,775 --> 00:45:06,577
(Tension in the air)

965
00:45:13,418 --> 00:45:14,852
- Mine!
- Na Yeon!

966
00:45:15,320 --> 00:45:16,787
- Mine!
- Na Yeon!

967
00:45:18,257 --> 00:45:19,157
Hey!

968
00:45:20,292 --> 00:45:23,494
(The set is too far!)

969
00:45:36,575 --> 00:45:39,577
The final score is 11 to 15.

970
00:45:39,578 --> 00:45:41,145
Set score of two to three.

971
00:45:41,146 --> 00:45:44,382
Shujitsu High School takes
a come-from-behind victory.

972
00:45:50,656 --> 00:45:51,656
Sorry.

973
00:45:53,292 --> 00:45:54,158
Let's go.

974
00:45:59,231 --> 00:46:02,266
Today's match was quite disappointing,
to be honest.

975
00:46:02,267 --> 00:46:03,901
We won the first two sets,

976
00:46:03,902 --> 00:46:08,606
and there were plenty of chances to win.

977
00:46:09,274 --> 00:46:11,308
Today's defeat...

978
00:46:12,110 --> 00:46:13,444
is really a bummer.

979
00:46:14,112 --> 00:46:15,179
Gosh, my legs.

980
00:46:18,250 --> 00:46:19,450
It's never easy.

981
00:46:23,222 --> 00:46:25,123
I thought we were going to end it
three to zero.

982
00:46:50,882 --> 00:46:55,315
(The cheers and applause felt like
they'd always be for me.)

983
00:47:02,301 --> 00:47:06,435
(The losing scene...)

984
00:47:10,035 --> 00:47:16,368
(I never wanted to see again.)

985
00:47:26,868 --> 00:47:28,468
Where should we start over?

986
00:47:29,735 --> 00:47:31,335
If we lose two more games,
we'll be disbanded.

987
00:47:31,901 --> 00:47:33,935
Maybe we'll be disbanded soon
at this rate.

988
00:47:39,101 --> 00:47:42,035
(The players gathered in the locker room
after the defeat.)

989
00:47:47,601 --> 00:47:49,501
This is really driving me crazy.

990
00:47:53,135 --> 00:47:59,168
(The come-from-behind loss
that's hard to believe)

991
00:48:00,968 --> 00:48:02,668
How can we ever beat other teams...

992
00:48:03,601 --> 00:48:07,601
when we lost to a high school team?

993
00:48:08,068 --> 00:48:09,101
This is no joke.

994
00:48:09,601 --> 00:48:13,268
We can only lose one more time now.

995
00:48:14,301 --> 00:48:15,368
Right?

996
00:48:16,768 --> 00:48:18,635
If we lose two more matches,
we'll be disbanded.

997
00:48:30,401 --> 00:48:34,301
I just didn't want
to think about anything.

998
00:48:37,001 --> 00:48:39,701
"What am I doing here? For what?"

999
00:48:41,001 --> 00:48:45,735
I was really worried
about the remaining games.

1000
00:48:48,968 --> 00:48:50,135
Where's my chair?

1001
00:48:53,035 --> 00:48:54,101
Let me sit down.

1002
00:49:00,668 --> 00:49:02,801
We recorded another loss today.

1003
00:49:03,701 --> 00:49:05,935
The Wonder Dogs have now added
another loss.

1004
00:49:07,035 --> 00:49:09,138
(If they lose four matches,
they will be disbanded.)

1005
00:49:10,135 --> 00:49:11,935
(Now, they have two defeats.)

1006
00:49:15,368 --> 00:49:17,135
What do you think of today's match?

1007
00:49:18,468 --> 00:49:20,168
Chae Rim, what do you think?

1008
00:49:20,835 --> 00:49:21,701
Tell me.

1009
00:49:23,401 --> 00:49:25,801
I think we could've done better.

1010
00:49:25,801 --> 00:49:26,968
- You think so?
- Yes.

1011
00:49:28,168 --> 00:49:31,701
Young In, and the others, tell me
what you think about the match.

1012
00:49:32,601 --> 00:49:34,501
It was disappointing for me too.

1013
00:49:34,768 --> 00:49:35,735
Disappointing?

1014
00:49:39,135 --> 00:49:40,068
What about the rest?

1015
00:49:40,668 --> 00:49:42,235
I want to hear
from the players who played today.

1016
00:49:50,901 --> 00:49:52,001
Speak up!

1017
00:49:53,201 --> 00:49:54,168
Those who played in the match!

1018
00:49:55,368 --> 00:49:56,501
I told you to share your thoughts.

1019
00:49:58,301 --> 00:50:03,168
There were many small, unseen mistakes,

1020
00:50:03,168 --> 00:50:08,031
and if we had avoided those,
the result might have been different.

1021
00:50:11,368 --> 00:50:16,235
I hope that everyone,

1022
00:50:16,235 --> 00:50:19,535
whether you played today or not,

1023
00:50:20,001 --> 00:50:23,435
can learn something from this game...

1024
00:50:23,735 --> 00:50:29,301
instead of just feeling disappointed.

1025
00:50:29,668 --> 00:50:32,817
Today's match was really frustrating,
and we're feeling that disappointment now.

1026
00:50:33,235 --> 00:50:35,768
I hope each of you can prepare better...

1027
00:50:35,768 --> 00:50:38,635
so that situations like this
don't happen again...

1028
00:50:38,935 --> 00:50:43,868
and we never feel this way again.

1029
00:50:43,868 --> 00:50:46,068
(After today's defeat,
they need to become stronger.)

1030
00:50:54,668 --> 00:50:57,668
I felt a bit embarrassed.

1031
00:50:58,235 --> 00:51:00,901
Our opponents were a high school team.

1032
00:51:00,901 --> 00:51:08,535
We were leading 2 to 0,
but ended up losing 3 to 2.

1033
00:51:11,001 --> 00:51:13,468
As their coach,

1034
00:51:13,468 --> 00:51:17,235
that was both embarrassing
and a little shameful.

1035
00:51:17,601 --> 00:51:19,335
It was very disappointing.

1036
00:51:21,435 --> 00:51:23,801
I'll announce the next opponents.

1037
00:51:30,935 --> 00:51:33,235
(Wonder Dogs' current win rate)

1038
00:51:35,935 --> 00:51:38,601
(If they get two more defeats,)

1039
00:51:38,601 --> 00:51:41,168
(the team itself will be disbanded.)

1040
00:51:41,468 --> 00:51:44,868
(The next opposing team they must beat)

1041
00:51:46,535 --> 00:51:49,701
(Choi Seong Wu,
the coach of Kwangju Women's University)

1042
00:51:49,968 --> 00:51:51,768
- Aren't you taking this too lightly?
- No!

1043
00:51:51,768 --> 00:51:53,268
- Is it over?
- No.

1044
00:51:53,601 --> 00:51:56,435
- Does it seem to be over to you?
- No, it's not over!

1045
00:51:59,368 --> 00:52:02,935
You conceded a couple of points
with that irresponsible play!

1046
00:52:03,801 --> 00:52:06,668
- Have a sense of responsibility!
- Let's go!

1047
00:52:09,368 --> 00:52:11,206
(Outstanding Coach Award
at National University Tournaments...)

1048
00:52:11,207 --> 00:52:12,335
(in 2023 and 2024)

1049
00:52:12,336 --> 00:52:13,868
(Best Coach Award at the U-Leauge in 2024)

1050
00:52:13,868 --> 00:52:17,168
(Choi Seong Wu, the rookie coach
who was born in 1992.)

1051
00:52:20,552 --> 00:52:22,566
(Kwangju Women's University
Volleyball Team)

1052
00:52:24,122 --> 00:52:26,389
(The average age of the players is 20.2.)

1053
00:52:26,922 --> 00:52:29,922
Because they're young,
they aren't afraid of anything.

1054
00:52:32,222 --> 00:52:35,422
I haven't seen a team
that trains harder than ours.

1055
00:52:35,755 --> 00:52:38,089
Our training lasts
about eight hours a day.

1056
00:52:38,089 --> 00:52:39,555
The players have been giving
up their vacations...

1057
00:52:39,555 --> 00:52:44,447
and training every day until 10 p.m.,
except for meal times.

1058
00:52:45,261 --> 00:52:49,295
It hasn't even been a month
since the Wonder Dogs were formed.

1059
00:52:49,855 --> 00:52:52,555
I'm sure they'll struggle a lot.

1060
00:52:53,289 --> 00:52:57,689
(The Wonder Dogs
vs. Kwangju Women's University)

1061
00:53:05,655 --> 00:53:07,089
Wrap it up.

1062
00:53:16,022 --> 00:53:18,122
I said I felt like
we were on the edge of a cliff.

1063
00:53:19,555 --> 00:53:21,422
Now, we've been pushed
to the edge, for real.

1064
00:53:23,055 --> 00:53:25,089
I resolved to do whatever it takes...

1065
00:53:26,022 --> 00:53:30,155
in the remaining matches
and to make sure we win the next one.

1066
00:53:30,822 --> 00:53:32,889
I must push through and win.

1067
00:53:33,255 --> 00:53:35,689
I believe that we've had
the best training...

1068
00:53:37,155 --> 00:53:39,955
and want to play well and win.

1069
00:53:42,989 --> 00:53:45,322
We'll review our previous game.

1070
00:53:45,322 --> 00:53:46,289
(Video meeting after returning)

1071
00:53:46,555 --> 00:53:51,055
Now, we're going to review the match
against Shujitsu High School.

1072
00:53:51,422 --> 00:53:56,089
We recorded 22 blocks.

1073
00:53:56,089 --> 00:53:58,522
That's almost enough to win a whole set
just with blocking.

1074
00:53:59,089 --> 00:54:02,955
That means our blocking was
really effective.

1075
00:54:03,389 --> 00:54:07,822
I've never seen a team
that made 22 blocks in a match in my life.

1076
00:54:08,755 --> 00:54:12,689
Twenty-two blocks is an incredible number.

1077
00:54:12,689 --> 00:54:14,722
But even with such an incredible number,

1078
00:54:14,722 --> 00:54:15,922
the reason we lost was...

1079
00:54:16,455 --> 00:54:21,422
that our attack success rate was
relatively low.

1080
00:54:22,589 --> 00:54:25,622
(Attack success rate: 32 percent)

1081
00:54:25,622 --> 00:54:27,022
No matter how well we keep the ball alive,

1082
00:54:27,022 --> 00:54:31,055
we can only score if we attack.

1083
00:54:31,055 --> 00:54:34,155
Right now, there are many things
we're failing at regarding this.

1084
00:54:34,155 --> 00:54:38,622
The score was 16 to 17,
with us trailing by 1 point.

1085
00:54:38,922 --> 00:54:44,087
This is the moment when we need to score,
since we're behind by a point.

1086
00:54:45,055 --> 00:54:46,022
Listen carefully.

1087
00:54:49,065 --> 00:54:51,422
The ball came over, and we received it.

1088
00:54:51,422 --> 00:54:52,489
And she set it up.

1089
00:54:52,489 --> 00:54:53,355
Stop.

1090
00:54:55,289 --> 00:54:56,389
Who is that in front of you?

1091
00:54:58,589 --> 00:54:59,589
Who is it?

1092
00:55:01,789 --> 00:55:02,855
The setter.

1093
00:55:05,555 --> 00:55:09,955
(She emphasized dozens of times
to hit it straight,)

1094
00:55:12,455 --> 00:55:15,422
You kept hitting it cross
into the opponent's block.

1095
00:55:15,889 --> 00:55:17,522
What on earth was going on?

1096
00:55:18,389 --> 00:55:19,922
Explain what was going on.

1097
00:55:26,122 --> 00:55:27,222
Explain.

1098
00:55:31,189 --> 00:55:34,722
That was a high ball,
so I tried to hit it long.

1099
00:55:43,289 --> 00:55:44,189
And?

1100
00:55:47,222 --> 00:55:50,422
But the swing was too short.

1101
00:55:51,489 --> 00:55:53,089
That can't be an excuse.

1102
00:55:53,089 --> 00:55:54,622
That's ridiculous.

1103
00:55:54,622 --> 00:55:56,555
Does it make sense to you?

1104
00:55:57,955 --> 00:55:59,722
Does it? What do you think?

1105
00:55:59,989 --> 00:56:01,589
Your swing was too short? What?

1106
00:56:03,955 --> 00:56:08,955
How can you even win a point...

1107
00:56:08,955 --> 00:56:10,789
if you make such a weird choice?

1108
00:56:12,989 --> 00:56:16,489
This is what we need to understand.

1109
00:56:16,489 --> 00:56:18,789
You must understand it
before playing on the court.

1110
00:56:19,522 --> 00:56:23,455
I want you to think about it more
when you're training too.

1111
00:56:24,355 --> 00:56:25,255
Do you get it?

1112
00:56:26,189 --> 00:56:31,855
I have a goal for this match
against Kwangju Women's University.

1113
00:56:32,955 --> 00:56:35,022
I have a goal.

1114
00:56:36,661 --> 00:56:38,061
I want to win 3 to 0, no matter what.

1115
00:56:38,062 --> 00:56:41,400
(A shutout victory
with the score of three to zero)

1116
00:56:41,588 --> 00:56:46,455
I want you to keep that goal in mind
as you prepare for the match.

1117
00:56:46,455 --> 00:56:48,422
- Yes.
- Got it?

1118
00:56:49,188 --> 00:56:50,955
It's late. Go eat something.

1119
00:56:50,955 --> 00:56:52,088
(The review meeting ends.)

1120
00:56:53,355 --> 00:56:55,755
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1121
00:56:56,622 --> 00:56:58,688
Except you, Enkhsoyol.
You're staying here.

1122
00:56:59,322 --> 00:57:00,388
Yes.

1123
00:57:07,315 --> 00:57:10,081
What do you think about it?

1124
00:57:10,568 --> 00:57:11,568
Your performance?

1125
00:57:11,971 --> 00:57:13,105
(Hesitating)

1126
00:57:13,106 --> 00:57:14,972
- What?
- I'm not doing great.

1127
00:57:14,972 --> 00:57:16,372
- Not doing great?
- Yes.

1128
00:57:16,372 --> 00:57:20,239
You can't just conclude
that you're not doing great.

1129
00:57:20,644 --> 00:57:23,144
I don't know what you're thinking
when you're playing volleyball.

1130
00:57:23,145 --> 00:57:24,478
I just don't understand.

1131
00:57:24,672 --> 00:57:28,439
You're supposed to make me
accept your choice.

1132
00:57:28,439 --> 00:57:31,372
But do you think you made
the right decision?

1133
00:57:34,306 --> 00:57:36,806
I want you to attack, right?

1134
00:57:36,806 --> 00:57:37,972
- Attack to score.
- Yes.

1135
00:57:37,972 --> 00:57:39,906
Let's say we're struggling.

1136
00:57:39,906 --> 00:57:41,406
If I were you,

1137
00:57:42,006 --> 00:57:44,572
I would be ready
even before there's a substitution.

1138
00:57:45,339 --> 00:57:46,772
Check who's at the front...

1139
00:57:46,772 --> 00:57:47,972
and who's at the back.

1140
00:57:48,272 --> 00:57:49,806
Where will you attack when you're in?

1141
00:57:49,806 --> 00:57:51,239
(She'd plan thoroughly
from outside the court.)

1142
00:57:51,239 --> 00:57:52,739
- Think of that before you step in.
- Yes, Coach.

1143
00:57:52,739 --> 00:57:53,872
After substitution,

1144
00:57:54,172 --> 00:57:55,272
look at the front.

1145
00:57:56,039 --> 00:57:57,272
Check where the defenders are.

1146
00:57:57,706 --> 00:57:59,506
You can think, "The front is better."

1147
00:57:59,992 --> 00:58:01,058
"I must make a point there."

1148
00:58:02,272 --> 00:58:07,506
I wasn't confident enough
to score immediately.

1149
00:58:08,572 --> 00:58:11,372
That's an excuse.

1150
00:58:12,406 --> 00:58:14,939
Let's not make excuses now.

1151
00:58:16,272 --> 00:58:17,272
Yes.

1152
00:58:21,139 --> 00:58:22,506
Do you have anything to say?

1153
00:58:22,506 --> 00:58:23,672
Or a question?

1154
00:58:27,039 --> 00:58:28,239
None.

1155
00:58:28,239 --> 00:58:29,339
- None?
- Yes.

1156
00:58:29,339 --> 00:58:32,039
Nothing at all?
What about the review there?

1157
00:58:32,039 --> 00:58:34,139
You don't want to ask anything?

1158
00:58:36,606 --> 00:58:38,039
I guess not.

1159
00:58:38,039 --> 00:58:39,539
- Nothing to ask.
- Then go.

1160
00:58:39,539 --> 00:58:41,139
- Go have your meal.
- Yes.

1161
00:58:47,006 --> 00:58:48,272
Thank you, Coach.

1162
00:58:48,272 --> 00:58:49,439
(Drinking water helplessly)

1163
00:58:50,039 --> 00:58:52,972
(Enkhsoyol leaves.)

1164
00:58:57,006 --> 00:59:01,072
She didn't seem determined
to do something.

1165
00:59:01,072 --> 00:59:04,506
So I got really angry.

1166
00:59:04,506 --> 00:59:08,139
"Coach, this is my fault,
but I can do better."

1167
00:59:08,139 --> 00:59:10,406
"Please give me another chance.
I'll try my best."

1168
00:59:10,406 --> 00:59:13,672
I wanted Enkhsoyol to act like this.

1169
00:59:14,172 --> 00:59:15,839
Does she want to play or not?

1170
00:59:16,106 --> 00:59:19,906
I was speechless at that moment.

1171
00:59:20,606 --> 00:59:26,672
"I'll make sure not to repeat my mistake."

1172
00:59:26,672 --> 00:59:28,206
That's what I wanted to say.

1173
00:59:28,206 --> 00:59:29,706
Yet, I couldn't say anything.

1174
00:59:30,139 --> 00:59:32,739
(The truth is...)

1175
00:59:33,572 --> 00:59:37,539
(Enkhsoyol did individual training...)

1176
00:59:37,972 --> 00:59:39,372
(and went running every night.)

1177
00:59:39,372 --> 00:59:41,072
(Sweaty)

1178
00:59:41,672 --> 00:59:43,572
(In the dormitory,)

1179
00:59:43,572 --> 00:59:46,239
(she wrote diary entries
about her volleyball practice...)

1180
00:59:48,006 --> 00:59:51,806
(every day with diligence.)

1181
00:59:51,806 --> 00:59:54,039
In case I forget,

1182
00:59:54,039 --> 00:59:56,506
I wrote down my exercise logs,

1183
00:59:56,506 --> 00:59:59,406
activities I did and the times,

1184
00:59:59,406 --> 01:00:04,206
and what I learned in the end.

1185
01:00:05,506 --> 01:00:07,006
("You did, and you're doing great.")

1186
01:00:07,006 --> 01:00:09,172
("And you'll do better.")

1187
01:00:09,706 --> 01:00:13,039
(But the rookie coach's
training wasn't easy.)

1188
01:00:13,039 --> 01:00:14,206
- Don't step out!
- Yes!

1189
01:00:14,206 --> 01:00:15,506
- Hit it deeper.
- Yes.

1190
01:00:15,506 --> 01:00:17,039
You must hit deep for efficient attacks.

1191
01:00:17,039 --> 01:00:18,072
Yes.

1192
01:00:18,072 --> 01:00:20,572
That's the only bad thing
I learned in Korea.

1193
01:00:20,572 --> 01:00:22,406
I say "Yes" before I know it.

1194
01:00:22,406 --> 01:00:25,206
I speak that word as if I understood.

1195
01:00:25,206 --> 01:00:28,839
I don't know why, but I'm having
a hard time because of this.

1196
01:00:31,039 --> 01:00:35,072
I first came to Korea
in tenth grade to play volleyball.

1197
01:00:35,072 --> 01:00:38,872
("I want to be a pro volleyball player
in the future.")

1198
01:00:39,472 --> 01:00:42,239
They said a player's career ends fast.

1199
01:00:42,606 --> 01:00:46,406
And they kept asking
if that's what I really wanted to do.

1200
01:00:47,106 --> 01:00:48,972
That was the only time
in the tenth grade...

1201
01:00:48,972 --> 01:00:50,839
when I wanted to go back to Mongolia.

1202
01:00:52,839 --> 01:00:57,106
But my family wouldn't want me
to come back too soon.

1203
01:00:57,639 --> 01:01:01,272
I thought it wasn't right,
so I held myself back.

1204
01:01:01,772 --> 01:01:04,772
(Enkhsoyol's mother was
a volleyball player.)

1205
01:01:05,206 --> 01:01:08,239
(She wanted to make her mother proud.)

1206
01:01:08,239 --> 01:01:12,172
There were many difficult times
after I graduated.

1207
01:01:12,439 --> 01:01:14,106
I wanted to join a pro team,

1208
01:01:15,006 --> 01:01:16,872
but I was rejected
because of my nationality.

1209
01:01:19,972 --> 01:01:25,039
(But she didn't give up, and while keeping
her dream to be a pro player,)

1210
01:01:26,172 --> 01:01:28,539
"This is a great opportunity!"

1211
01:01:29,039 --> 01:01:30,806
That's what I thought.

1212
01:01:30,806 --> 01:01:34,106
(she got the opportunity
to join the Wonder Dogs.)

1213
01:01:34,106 --> 01:01:37,439
I believe that if I try harder,

1214
01:01:37,439 --> 01:01:40,639
then I might get a chance.

1215
01:01:40,639 --> 01:01:42,472
(She didn't give up her dream
to be a pro volleyball player.)

1216
01:01:42,472 --> 01:01:47,506
I was a bit upset until yesterday.

1217
01:01:47,506 --> 01:01:51,539
If I talk to the coach...

1218
01:01:51,539 --> 01:01:55,539
and improve myself,
I guess it will be okay.

1219
01:01:55,539 --> 01:02:00,806
(Training day for a match
against Kwangju Women's University)

1220
01:02:05,139 --> 01:02:08,906
(Going strict from the start)

1221
01:02:09,772 --> 01:02:12,472
(Their goal is a shutout victory.)

1222
01:02:12,472 --> 01:02:14,139
We must really win this time.

1223
01:02:14,139 --> 01:02:15,806
We should make it no matter what.

1224
01:02:15,806 --> 01:02:17,806
Our team can't lose again
but win at all costs.

1225
01:02:18,206 --> 01:02:20,506
We'll never repeat what we've done.

1226
01:02:20,506 --> 01:02:22,172
I was determined to fight.

1227
01:02:23,372 --> 01:02:27,106
I'll save the Wonder Dogs from danger.

1228
01:02:27,739 --> 01:02:28,839
Here I go!

1229
01:02:30,972 --> 01:02:32,139
It hurts!

1230
01:02:32,139 --> 01:02:34,672
(Players continue to train
even after the session.)

1231
01:02:35,306 --> 01:02:37,272
Let's go home!

1232
01:02:37,839 --> 01:02:39,306
(Glancing)

1233
01:02:39,639 --> 01:02:41,906
(She spots Enkhsoyol drinking water.)

1234
01:02:42,239 --> 01:02:43,906
Come here, Enkhsoyol.

1235
01:02:45,372 --> 01:02:47,606
(Rushing)

1236
01:02:49,939 --> 01:02:52,339
(She gets nervous...)

1237
01:02:52,339 --> 01:02:54,839
(when the coach calls her.)

1238
01:02:58,372 --> 01:03:00,239
Don't you want to play volleyball?

1239
01:03:01,639 --> 01:03:02,906
- Do you want to?
- Yes.

1240
01:03:02,906 --> 01:03:05,139
It doesn't look like you want to play.

1241
01:03:05,672 --> 01:03:10,439
We find a reason to do something
in our lives, right?

1242
01:03:11,039 --> 01:03:12,906
You can think of 100 reasons.

1243
01:03:13,339 --> 01:03:14,572
- An excuse?
- Well.

1244
01:03:14,572 --> 01:03:15,739
A reason or an excuse.

1245
01:03:15,739 --> 01:03:18,472
That's a loser's mindset.

1246
01:03:18,839 --> 01:03:23,006
Enkhsoyol, if you keep
making excuses or reasons,

1247
01:03:23,506 --> 01:03:24,672
your mind will be like a loser.

1248
01:03:25,406 --> 01:03:28,272
(Imitating a loser)

1249
01:03:28,572 --> 01:03:30,639
I don't want to see that weak side.

1250
01:03:30,639 --> 01:03:31,839
- Understood?
- Yes.

1251
01:03:31,839 --> 01:03:33,906
Try to believe in yourself.

1252
01:03:34,272 --> 01:03:35,739
You're good enough.

1253
01:03:36,639 --> 01:03:39,306
Don't compromise.

1254
01:03:39,806 --> 01:03:40,839
Do you know what that means?

1255
01:03:41,439 --> 01:03:43,572
(Compromise?)

1256
01:03:44,039 --> 01:03:47,839
Stop making excuses.

1257
01:03:48,739 --> 01:03:51,206
Instead of excuses,
come up with solutions.

1258
01:03:51,572 --> 01:03:52,606
For yourself.

1259
01:03:53,006 --> 01:03:56,239
"Too bad I couldn't do this."

1260
01:03:56,239 --> 01:04:00,772
"I'll try this, so I can play
better next time."

1261
01:04:00,772 --> 01:04:02,172
You can think of these to solve problems.

1262
01:04:02,172 --> 01:04:04,339
Change excuses to solutions.

1263
01:04:04,339 --> 01:04:07,072
Your mindset itself must be changed.

1264
01:04:07,072 --> 01:04:08,706
That's how you'll be a great player.

1265
01:04:09,239 --> 01:04:11,372
- Will you just stay here like this?
- No, Coach.

1266
01:04:11,372 --> 01:04:13,172
Right. You should go to bigger places.

1267
01:04:13,172 --> 01:04:15,372
To do that, you need to think big.

1268
01:04:15,899 --> 01:04:17,072
It won't be easy for you to get there.

1269
01:04:17,672 --> 01:04:18,706
Nobody can.

1270
01:04:18,706 --> 01:04:20,939
Do you think people there joined
without a reason?

1271
01:04:20,939 --> 01:04:22,572
No. They went through a lot.

1272
01:04:22,572 --> 01:04:24,072
You may have struggled,

1273
01:04:24,072 --> 01:04:26,239
but some went through much worse.

1274
01:04:26,239 --> 01:04:27,772
You've got this.

1275
01:04:27,772 --> 01:04:29,206
- Go for it.
- Yes.

1276
01:04:29,839 --> 01:04:32,139
I'll help you, okay?

1277
01:04:32,472 --> 01:04:38,172
I think I was more concerned with her
than anyone.

1278
01:04:38,639 --> 01:04:42,072
No player should be left behind.

1279
01:04:42,806 --> 01:04:47,906
She made many impressive attacks
during the tryout.

1280
01:04:47,906 --> 01:04:49,339
Enkhsoyol is good.

1281
01:04:49,339 --> 01:04:51,872
With that skill, we should help her
get citizenship.

1282
01:04:51,872 --> 01:04:53,172
She surprised me.

1283
01:04:53,172 --> 01:04:55,806
I'm sure she could even be
a starter on a pro team.

1284
01:04:56,072 --> 01:04:59,106
The reason we chose Enkhsoyol is...

1285
01:04:59,106 --> 01:05:01,639
because of her attacks.

1286
01:05:01,972 --> 01:05:05,239
(The Wonder Dogs continued to lose.)

1287
01:05:06,006 --> 01:05:12,039
(It's due to their low success rates
in attacks.)

1288
01:05:12,972 --> 01:05:14,172
I should have replaced Chae Rim.

1289
01:05:14,172 --> 01:05:15,639
She did look exhausted.

1290
01:05:15,639 --> 01:05:17,239
We should have put Enkhsoyol in.

1291
01:05:20,339 --> 01:05:22,306
If she becomes active in attacks,

1292
01:05:22,306 --> 01:05:24,006
she might earn many points.

1293
01:05:24,306 --> 01:05:27,572
So I believe Enkhsoyol is
important in our team.

1294
01:05:28,939 --> 01:05:31,006
(Training focused on Enkhsoyol)

1295
01:05:31,006 --> 01:05:32,706
Enkhsoyol, the ball is dropping.

1296
01:05:33,072 --> 01:05:34,406
In 1, 2!

1297
01:05:35,572 --> 01:05:37,172
Let's go!

1298
01:05:37,172 --> 01:05:38,872
Use your full strength.

1299
01:05:38,872 --> 01:05:40,606
Hit it deep with all you've got.

1300
01:05:40,606 --> 01:05:41,739
Go in.

1301
01:05:41,739 --> 01:05:43,239
Deeper.

1302
01:05:43,239 --> 01:05:44,439
Stronger.

1303
01:05:44,439 --> 01:05:45,706
That's it!

1304
01:05:45,906 --> 01:05:46,939
Enkhsoyol.

1305
01:05:47,306 --> 01:05:48,672
Nice attack.

1306
01:05:49,006 --> 01:05:53,506
Hit it with more power.

1307
01:05:53,506 --> 01:05:55,206
(Coach Kim pushes her more.)

1308
01:05:56,839 --> 01:05:59,872
Come on!

1309
01:05:59,872 --> 01:06:02,039
(Messy hair)

1310
01:06:02,539 --> 01:06:03,539
One more time.

1311
01:06:04,272 --> 01:06:05,972
(It's all up to Enkhsoyol's right arm.)

1312
01:06:05,972 --> 01:06:07,639
Great. Hit it like that.

1313
01:06:08,772 --> 01:06:09,839
That's it!

1314
01:06:11,639 --> 01:06:13,739
What will you do? Nice one!

1315
01:06:14,406 --> 01:06:16,439
(Let's go defeat
Kwangju Women's University!)

1316
01:06:16,839 --> 01:06:20,072
(The match day)

1317
01:06:22,172 --> 01:06:24,839
(Cheongju Gymnasium)

1318
01:06:25,572 --> 01:06:28,139
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1319
01:06:34,039 --> 01:06:35,039
We should do well.

1320
01:06:36,986 --> 01:06:40,386
(The locker room is tense.)

1321
01:06:41,219 --> 01:06:42,952
(Knocking)

1322
01:06:46,486 --> 01:06:48,186
Well, we...

1323
01:06:48,986 --> 01:06:51,352
I'm announcing the starting lineup.

1324
01:06:51,352 --> 01:06:52,986
There's a little change...

1325
01:06:53,419 --> 01:06:56,452
on the left.

1326
01:06:57,619 --> 01:06:58,619
Seung Ju will be on the left,

1327
01:07:00,152 --> 01:07:01,719
and Chae Rim on the right.

1328
01:07:03,152 --> 01:07:06,252
Na Hee and Myoung Hwa are in the middle.

1329
01:07:06,619 --> 01:07:09,286
The setters will be Na Yeon and Hye In.

1330
01:07:10,519 --> 01:07:12,752
And on the left,

1331
01:07:13,752 --> 01:07:15,986
- the outside hitter will be Enkhsoyol.
- Got it?

1332
01:07:17,586 --> 01:07:20,019
I'm so grateful to Coach for trusting me.

1333
01:07:20,019 --> 01:07:23,319
I want to show her my confidence.

1334
01:07:24,286 --> 01:07:28,519
I could see her striving during practice.

1335
01:07:28,519 --> 01:07:32,419
I'm looking forward to her match today.

1336
01:07:34,719 --> 01:07:37,152
The match against the Japanese team
ended with much regret...

1337
01:07:37,152 --> 01:07:39,052
and their second consecutive loss.

1338
01:07:39,052 --> 01:07:40,219
Now, the Wonder Dogs,

1339
01:07:40,219 --> 01:07:42,652
in crisis, are facing their fourth match.

1340
01:07:42,652 --> 01:07:44,552
Today, commentator Lee Suk Ja joins us.

1341
01:07:44,552 --> 01:07:46,252
- Hello.
- Hello.

1342
01:07:46,252 --> 01:07:48,986
The team Wonder Dogs are up against today,
with one win and two losses,

1343
01:07:48,986 --> 01:07:51,319
is the strongest college team,
Kwangju Women's University.

1344
01:07:51,319 --> 01:07:54,852
As soon as they were formed,
they've been sweeping the U-League,

1345
01:07:54,852 --> 01:07:56,586
setting great records.

1346
01:07:56,586 --> 01:08:00,186
Plus, they also have a young,
rookie coach.

1347
01:08:00,186 --> 01:08:02,252
They're truly a team full of passion.

1348
01:08:02,252 --> 01:08:05,052
(The rookie powerhouse
of the U-League appeared like a comet.)

1349
01:08:08,519 --> 01:08:11,452
(Glancing)

1350
01:08:17,752 --> 01:08:21,052
To start with, Eun Jin is
a professional player.

1351
01:08:21,052 --> 01:08:24,086
She also has a knack
for reading her coach's mind.

1352
01:08:24,086 --> 01:08:28,286
That's why Setter Eun Jin was chosen first
when the team was formed.

1353
01:08:28,286 --> 01:08:29,319
That's right.

1354
01:08:29,752 --> 01:08:32,186
As for Na Hyeon, she was even honored...

1355
01:08:32,186 --> 01:08:34,186
as MVP in the U-League.

1356
01:08:35,186 --> 01:08:37,286
That's why Wonder Dogs...

1357
01:08:37,286 --> 01:08:39,386
can't let their guard down
against this team.

1358
01:08:39,386 --> 01:08:41,252
They can't let them win here, can they?

1359
01:08:41,252 --> 01:08:43,752
We're joined
by Kwangju Women's University supporters.

1360
01:08:43,752 --> 01:08:45,186
Among them is alumna...

1361
01:08:45,186 --> 01:08:48,452
and Olympic gold medalist An San.

1362
01:08:48,819 --> 01:08:51,286
But Wonder Dogs have
their own supporters too.

1363
01:08:51,286 --> 01:08:52,319
- Especially, they have Manager Boo.
- Let's go!

1364
01:08:52,319 --> 01:08:54,286
- He's cheering hard for them.
- Nice.

1365
01:08:54,286 --> 01:08:55,286
(Manager Boo is here!)

1366
01:08:57,952 --> 01:09:00,619
Guys, let's raise our voices
as we warm up.

1367
01:09:01,286 --> 01:09:02,952
(Marching)

1368
01:09:02,952 --> 01:09:03,886
Ball!

1369
01:09:06,152 --> 01:09:07,286
Hey!

1370
01:09:07,852 --> 01:09:10,019
Hey! Good.

1371
01:09:11,919 --> 01:09:12,952
Hey! Come!

1372
01:09:13,586 --> 01:09:14,452
Yes!

1373
01:09:15,352 --> 01:09:16,452
Open your mouth!

1374
01:09:16,452 --> 01:09:19,019
Go! Hey! Give it to me!

1375
01:09:19,352 --> 01:09:23,619
In his second year, Coach Choi Seong Wu
led the team to victory.

1376
01:09:23,619 --> 01:09:26,386
He's even the youngest
to be named Best Rookie.

1377
01:09:26,386 --> 01:09:27,219
Born in 1992.

1378
01:09:27,219 --> 01:09:29,452
Both coaches are young.

1379
01:09:29,452 --> 01:09:31,719
Especially, Coach Kim has just debuted,

1380
01:09:31,719 --> 01:09:34,586
while Coach Choi is a rising star
in the league.

1381
01:09:34,586 --> 01:09:35,886
- He's young.
- Indeed.

1382
01:09:35,886 --> 01:09:38,486
I can't wait to see
today's strategy battle between the two.

1383
01:09:41,286 --> 01:09:43,952
(Taking off his glasses)

1384
01:09:43,952 --> 01:09:47,752
Maybe today, we'll hear
the coaches shouting louder...

1385
01:09:47,752 --> 01:09:52,752
- than the players themselves on court.
- That's right.

1386
01:09:53,719 --> 01:09:57,019
Today, Wonder Dogs need a decisive win.

1387
01:09:57,019 --> 01:09:59,786
Exactly. Because the teams
they'll face next are...

1388
01:09:59,786 --> 01:10:01,186
the corporate team champion,

1389
01:10:01,186 --> 01:10:03,086
the pro runner-up team,

1390
01:10:03,086 --> 01:10:06,319
and the pro champion team.

1391
01:10:06,852 --> 01:10:08,319
That's why today's win...

1392
01:10:08,319 --> 01:10:10,886
matters more than ever.

1393
01:10:15,286 --> 01:10:17,552
- Good luck today.
- Good luck.

1394
01:10:19,119 --> 01:10:21,719
Let's check out Wonder Dogs' lineup.

1395
01:10:21,719 --> 01:10:22,819
Setter, Lee Na Yeon.

1396
01:10:22,819 --> 01:10:24,352
Outside hitter, Enkhsoyol.

1397
01:10:24,352 --> 01:10:25,952
Middle blocker, Moon Myoung Hwa.

1398
01:10:25,952 --> 01:10:27,652
Opposite hitter, Back Chae Rim.

1399
01:10:27,652 --> 01:10:29,452
Outside hitter, Pyo Seung Ju.

1400
01:10:29,452 --> 01:10:30,852
Middle blocker, Kim Na Hee.

1401
01:10:30,852 --> 01:10:32,552
And libero is Koo Hye In.

1402
01:10:32,552 --> 01:10:35,419
Now the lineup
of Kwangju Women's University.

1403
01:10:35,419 --> 01:10:36,752
Setter, Son Eun Jin.

1404
01:10:36,752 --> 01:10:38,219
Middle blocker, Kim Su Bin.

1405
01:10:38,219 --> 01:10:39,852
Outside hitter, Kim Ah Hyeon.

1406
01:10:39,852 --> 01:10:41,519
Opposite hitter, Kim Na Hyeon.

1407
01:10:41,519 --> 01:10:42,952
Middle blocker, Kim Yeon Hwa.

1408
01:10:42,952 --> 01:10:44,586
Outside hitter, Cha Ye Jin.

1409
01:10:44,586 --> 01:10:46,186
Libero, Bae Eun Mi.

1410
01:10:48,186 --> 01:10:50,852
- Let's go!
- Yes!

1411
01:10:51,186 --> 01:10:52,886
Getting ahead early in the set is crucial.

1412
01:10:52,886 --> 01:10:53,752
Let's take the lead.

1413
01:10:53,752 --> 01:10:55,986
Their morale is high in the beginning.

1414
01:10:55,986 --> 01:10:59,219
Let's focus on breaking their spirit now.

1415
01:10:59,219 --> 01:11:01,052
- All right.
- Okay.

1416
01:11:01,052 --> 01:11:03,452
Wonder Dogs are determined
to break their losing streak...

1417
01:11:03,452 --> 01:11:06,519
against the strongest team
in the U-League.

1418
01:11:06,786 --> 01:11:08,986
Today, they're aiming not just for a win,

1419
01:11:08,986 --> 01:11:13,252
but for a solid 3-0 victory.

1420
01:11:13,252 --> 01:11:18,119
Our team tends to start off...

1421
01:11:18,119 --> 01:11:20,319
by giving up a big lead.

1422
01:11:21,419 --> 01:11:23,752
(Wonder Dogs' first match)

1423
01:11:24,486 --> 01:11:27,052
(Against Geunyoung Girls' High,
they started four points behind.)

1424
01:11:27,419 --> 01:11:29,719
(Against Altos, eight points behind.)

1425
01:11:30,519 --> 01:11:33,619
(Against Shujitsu High School,
five points behind.)

1426
01:11:34,019 --> 01:11:36,119
(They've always been the chaser.)

1427
01:11:36,952 --> 01:11:39,152
Wonder Dogs have let their opponents
take the early lead every time.

1428
01:11:39,152 --> 01:11:42,919
This time, it's crucial
to take control from the start.

1429
01:11:43,119 --> 01:11:45,386
(We can't let them take
the lead this time.)

1430
01:11:45,386 --> 01:11:48,386
We're hoping Wonder Dogs...

1431
01:11:48,386 --> 01:11:51,286
will give their all
and finish strong today.

1432
01:11:51,286 --> 01:11:52,386
(We must take the lead this time,
no matter what.)

1433
01:11:53,619 --> 01:11:56,686
(Wonder Dogs,)

1434
01:11:56,686 --> 01:12:00,352
(vs. Kwangju Women's University)

1435
01:12:01,419 --> 01:12:03,452
(The first set begins.)

1436
01:12:03,886 --> 01:12:05,252
(The first serve is by Na Yeon.)

1437
01:12:05,252 --> 01:12:06,619
Serve by Na Yeon.

1438
01:12:06,619 --> 01:12:08,286
The match between the two teams begins.

1439
01:12:09,219 --> 01:12:10,352
Here she comes.@(Unclear)

1440
01:12:16,919 --> 01:12:17,886
The attack is...
successful.

1441
01:12:18,819 --> 01:12:20,652
(Touch out after hitting her hand)

1442
01:12:21,286 --> 01:12:22,686
- Again!
- Chae Rim!

1443
01:12:22,686 --> 01:12:23,986
- The ball was here.
- Yes.

1444
01:12:23,986 --> 01:12:25,486
Send it to the center.

1445
01:12:27,219 --> 01:12:32,286
(Coach Choi's loud and clear instruction
worked perfectly.)

1446
01:12:32,819 --> 01:12:34,752
The spike was by Na Hyeon,

1447
01:12:34,752 --> 01:12:37,619
who was the MVP...

1448
01:12:37,619 --> 01:12:39,586
- at the Goseong Tournament this year.
- That's right.

1449
01:12:40,552 --> 01:12:43,419
(Will they let their opponent
take the lead again?)

1450
01:12:43,419 --> 01:12:46,786
(First set, Kwangju Women's University 1
: Wonder Dogs 0)

1451
01:12:47,152 --> 01:12:48,519
Good. Look ahead.

1452
01:12:48,519 --> 01:12:50,552
There are three hitters!

1453
01:12:50,952 --> 01:12:53,719
Okay!

1454
01:12:54,044 --> 01:12:55,744
Hey! Serve Number Two!

1455
01:12:56,619 --> 01:12:57,552
Number Two!

1456
01:13:01,119 --> 01:13:02,419
(We'll score this time at any cost.)

1457
01:13:02,419 --> 01:13:04,419
Do the short serve! Do it right away!

1458
01:13:04,419 --> 01:13:06,852
(Serve by Su Bin)

1459
01:13:07,852 --> 01:13:08,786
Serve by Su Bin.

1460
01:13:09,519 --> 01:13:10,686
There they go! On the right!

1461
01:13:10,686 --> 01:13:11,619
Chae Rim's reception.
Underhand toss.

1462
01:13:12,986 --> 01:13:13,919
Spike!

1463
01:13:15,652 --> 01:13:17,786
(MVP Na Hyeon's attack)

1464
01:13:17,786 --> 01:13:18,752
Spike!

1465
01:13:20,252 --> 01:13:21,519
Score!

1466
01:13:21,519 --> 01:13:23,119
Myoung Hwa!

1467
01:13:23,119 --> 01:13:26,919
Myoung Hwa shows off her blocking
from the start!

1468
01:13:26,919 --> 01:13:28,619
(National flower is the Rose of Sharon!
The flower of volleyball is Myoung Hwa!)

1469
01:13:28,819 --> 01:13:29,952
Good!

1470
01:13:29,952 --> 01:13:31,552
(Standing up)

1471
01:13:32,352 --> 01:13:33,886
Good, Myoung Hwa!

1472
01:13:34,652 --> 01:13:38,552
(Myoung Hwa did it!)

1473
01:13:38,718 --> 01:13:41,277
She's never let us down.

1474
01:13:41,278 --> 01:13:43,619
She shows her signature block
right from the beginning.

1475
01:13:43,619 --> 01:13:45,919
(Moon Myoung Hwa)

1476
01:13:46,686 --> 01:13:49,186
(Bouncing)

1477
01:13:50,352 --> 01:13:54,119
(The next serve is Enkhsoyol.)

1478
01:13:56,219 --> 01:13:59,052
(Worried)

1479
01:14:00,086 --> 01:14:03,119
(It was her serve chance in the match
against Geunyoung Girls' High.)

1480
01:14:03,419 --> 01:14:05,852
(Serve by Enkhsoyol)

1481
01:14:06,286 --> 01:14:09,219
(The ball didn't cross the net.)

1482
01:14:09,852 --> 01:14:11,219
There's still a chance when it's out.

1483
01:14:11,219 --> 01:14:12,952
We still have a chance to receive.

1484
01:14:12,952 --> 01:14:14,386
But is there a chance
when it hits the net?

1485
01:14:14,386 --> 01:14:15,619
- No.
- No, right?

1486
01:14:16,319 --> 01:14:18,886
You can keep the rally going
with a long serve.

1487
01:14:19,386 --> 01:14:23,419
(That's how Enkhsoyol started training
with a focus on serving.)

1488
01:14:25,819 --> 01:14:28,486
(Please, Enkhsoyol.)

1489
01:14:28,486 --> 01:14:29,419
Serve.

1490
01:14:30,586 --> 01:14:32,219
(Seeing her serving form,
the coach gave her direct feedback.)

1491
01:14:32,219 --> 01:14:34,152
Use your palm!

1492
01:14:37,219 --> 01:14:39,219
(The intense training continued
until she got it right.)

1493
01:14:40,552 --> 01:14:41,452
(She finally succeeded in it.)

1494
01:14:41,452 --> 01:14:42,919
- Make it long!
- Okay!

1495
01:14:43,352 --> 01:14:45,619
(Unstoppable potential)

1496
01:14:47,619 --> 01:14:50,052
(Did she level up
thanks to Coach Kim's precise feedback?)

1497
01:14:50,652 --> 01:14:53,819
(Nervous)

1498
01:14:53,986 --> 01:14:54,819
Serve!

1499
01:14:58,119 --> 01:14:59,186
Enkhsoyol's serve.

1500
01:14:59,552 --> 01:15:00,719
A sharp serve lands in!

1501
01:15:01,052 --> 01:15:02,052
Nice!

1502
01:15:02,052 --> 01:15:03,086
One more time! One more!

1503
01:15:04,652 --> 01:15:06,019
No!

1504
01:15:06,019 --> 01:15:07,186
The ball crosses over the net hastily.

1505
01:15:07,186 --> 01:15:08,619
It's a chance! Seung Ju!

1506
01:15:11,152 --> 01:15:12,119
The center!@(Unclear)

1507
01:15:12,719 --> 01:15:13,619
Behind you!

1508
01:15:14,319 --> 01:15:15,352
(They change the formation,
exchanging mysterious signals.)

1509
01:15:15,352 --> 01:15:16,886
- Go to your position!
- Behind you!

1510
01:15:16,886 --> 01:15:18,186
Follow it!

1511
01:15:18,186 --> 01:15:20,786
Kwangju Women's University saves it.

1512
01:15:20,786 --> 01:15:21,686
It's another chance for Wonder Dogs.

1513
01:15:21,686 --> 01:15:23,186
Watch out for a quick attack!

1514
01:15:25,186 --> 01:15:28,186
(It's not a quick attack, but a set?)

1515
01:15:28,719 --> 01:15:29,652
Enkhsoyol!

1516
01:15:30,152 --> 01:15:31,819
(Enkhsoyol, it's your chance!)

1517
01:15:34,352 --> 01:15:36,219
Back attack!

1518
01:15:36,219 --> 01:15:37,352
Enkhsoyol!

1519
01:15:37,352 --> 01:15:39,186
(Standing up)

1520
01:15:39,186 --> 01:15:40,419
Well done!

1521
01:15:42,119 --> 01:15:44,019
- Nice!
- Well done.

1522
01:15:44,019 --> 01:15:45,386
Get ready for the next.

1523
01:15:46,186 --> 01:15:48,419
The attack worked perfectly...

1524
01:15:48,419 --> 01:15:49,819
as they utilized the back attack.

1525
01:15:49,819 --> 01:15:51,252
(Myoung Hwa feints a hit, while Enkhsoyol
strikes from the back row.)

1526
01:15:51,986 --> 01:15:53,352
Nice, Enkhsoyol!

1527
01:15:53,352 --> 01:15:57,786
As far as I know,
that's one of Coach Kim's strategies.

1528
01:15:58,486 --> 01:16:01,552
In this game, they'll be using
more back-row attacks.

1529
01:16:01,819 --> 01:16:04,519
(When you use the center
as a decoy for a back attack,)

1530
01:16:05,786 --> 01:16:08,486
(you can catch
the opposing middle blocker off guard.)

1531
01:16:09,452 --> 01:16:11,019
(Just as Yeon Koung planned,)

1532
01:16:11,019 --> 01:16:12,886
(the opponent was fooled and hesitated.)

1533
01:16:13,986 --> 01:16:15,986
(That's how the back attack
worked perfectly.)

1534
01:16:17,786 --> 01:16:20,552
(The rookie coach's strategy paid off.)

1535
01:16:21,119 --> 01:16:22,152
Thank you.

1536
01:16:22,152 --> 01:16:24,686
Wonder Dogs are showing
a variety of plays...

1537
01:16:24,686 --> 01:16:26,919
and continue to score.

1538
01:16:27,286 --> 01:16:29,419
Where did I tell you to move yesterday?

1539
01:16:29,919 --> 01:16:30,786
Hey!

1540
01:16:32,286 --> 01:16:34,019
(He noticed Enkhsoyol.)

1541
01:16:34,419 --> 01:16:35,290
Hey, Na Hyeon.

1542
01:16:35,487 --> 01:16:37,587
Step back and defend Enkhsoyol's balls.

1543
01:16:38,320 --> 01:16:39,353
Step back, guys.

1544
01:16:39,353 --> 01:16:43,953
(Enkhsoyol's serve to watch out)

1545
01:16:47,587 --> 01:16:48,420
Serve.

1546
01:16:50,020 --> 01:16:51,820
(Another strong serve)

1547
01:16:51,820 --> 01:16:52,653
They receive it.

1548
01:16:52,653 --> 01:16:54,353
Good. Send it to the back.

1549
01:16:54,787 --> 01:16:56,920
(Back set as instructed)

1550
01:16:57,787 --> 01:16:59,287
A roll shot, but it's blocked.

1551
01:17:00,287 --> 01:17:02,287
(Kwangju Women's University's
attack attempt)

1552
01:17:02,287 --> 01:17:03,353
Catch it!

1553
01:17:03,553 --> 01:17:04,353
Spike!

1554
01:17:04,353 --> 01:17:05,487
But they set it up again.

1555
01:17:05,887 --> 01:17:06,687
Na Yeon.

1556
01:17:07,987 --> 01:17:08,853
She hits it hard!

1557
01:17:09,153 --> 01:17:10,587
They're in a blocking formation.

1558
01:17:10,587 --> 01:17:11,553
Back set.

1559
01:17:13,587 --> 01:17:14,953
(Received again!)

1560
01:17:14,953 --> 01:17:15,887
The defense is set.

1561
01:17:18,487 --> 01:17:20,153
Go deep. Hit it long!

1562
01:17:20,153 --> 01:17:21,987
Guys, it's a roll shot!

1563
01:17:22,853 --> 01:17:25,220
(It is, and they make the dig.)

1564
01:17:29,487 --> 01:17:30,853
Right-side spike!

1565
01:17:32,387 --> 01:17:34,720
They call a touch-out.

1566
01:17:36,720 --> 01:17:38,587
We're seeing a lot of rallies right now.

1567
01:17:38,587 --> 01:17:41,953
The Kwangju Women's University players
have solid defense too.

1568
01:17:43,020 --> 01:17:44,520
Keep your eyes on number six.

1569
01:17:44,520 --> 01:17:48,187
(Almost as threatening
as Yeon Koung's spot-on tactics)

1570
01:17:48,553 --> 01:17:50,153
Soft hit coming! Watch out!

1571
01:17:50,653 --> 01:17:53,187
Coach Seung Wu's coaching is
quite intimidating.

1572
01:17:53,187 --> 01:17:55,120
Coach Seung Wu has his strategy,

1573
01:17:55,120 --> 01:17:56,720
and they're moving perfectly
according to it.

1574
01:17:58,787 --> 01:18:01,253
(Getting on their nerves)

1575
01:18:03,220 --> 01:18:04,887
Sorry. I'll set it up higher.

1576
01:18:06,753 --> 01:18:09,387
Set it more inside, Na Yeon.

1577
01:18:09,387 --> 01:18:10,253
Okay.

1578
01:18:12,953 --> 01:18:13,920
(Got the signal)

1579
01:18:13,920 --> 01:18:15,553
The score is tied, two to two.

1580
01:18:16,687 --> 01:18:19,820
Hit it hard! Watch out for the left side!

1581
01:18:19,820 --> 01:18:21,387
It's a tense start.

1582
01:18:23,587 --> 01:18:24,887
Ah Hyeon serving.

1583
01:18:27,720 --> 01:18:29,053
Go! Get it!

1584
01:18:30,753 --> 01:18:32,353
Seung Ju's push shot.

1585
01:18:32,353 --> 01:18:33,553
One, two. It's a tip!

1586
01:18:33,553 --> 01:18:34,953
Darn it...

1587
01:18:35,920 --> 01:18:36,820
Na Yeon.

1588
01:18:38,687 --> 01:18:39,753
(Rookie coach's tight battle)

1589
01:18:39,753 --> 01:18:42,220
It'll keep working. Go with it.

1590
01:18:45,487 --> 01:18:47,987
(Let's extend the lead.)

1591
01:18:48,420 --> 01:18:50,753
Looking forward to Myung Hwa's serve.

1592
01:18:50,953 --> 01:18:52,620
We have to catch first. Step in!

1593
01:18:57,187 --> 01:18:58,920
- Good.
- They receive it well.

1594
01:18:58,920 --> 01:18:59,987
Okay!

1595
01:18:59,987 --> 01:19:02,153
(MVP Na Hyeon's roll shot)

1596
01:19:02,653 --> 01:19:04,253
She drops to a knee for the dig.

1597
01:19:07,220 --> 01:19:09,420
Get in there. It's up. Go!

1598
01:19:10,920 --> 01:19:12,787
- Pass to C!
- Go!

1599
01:19:16,820 --> 01:19:18,353
Ye Jin's wonderful play.

1600
01:19:20,420 --> 01:19:21,320
Myung Hwa!

1601
01:19:22,553 --> 01:19:23,820
Come on! Stay focused!

1602
01:19:23,820 --> 01:19:25,453
We have to take the lead.
What are you doing?

1603
01:19:25,453 --> 01:19:27,020
Give it all your energy!

1604
01:19:28,653 --> 01:19:29,520
It's a miss.

1605
01:19:29,520 --> 01:19:33,287
In a situation like this,
the players really should...

1606
01:19:33,287 --> 01:19:36,853
catch it and make a good play out of it.

1607
01:19:37,853 --> 01:19:40,053
What are you doing in there, Myung Hwa?

1608
01:19:42,087 --> 01:19:43,220
Just take a break today.

1609
01:19:43,620 --> 01:19:44,620
You're on the bench today.

1610
01:19:46,387 --> 01:19:49,587
(It's serious when you don't score.)

1611
01:19:49,920 --> 01:19:52,520
Na Yeon, go further. Don't stop there.

1612
01:19:52,520 --> 01:19:53,420
To back C.

1613
01:19:54,687 --> 01:19:55,820
Back set.

1614
01:19:55,820 --> 01:19:56,987
Chae Rim!

1615
01:19:58,753 --> 01:20:00,953
We need more points, guys.

1616
01:20:01,587 --> 01:20:04,220
Keep your hands centered on the ball.

1617
01:20:04,220 --> 01:20:05,687
Do you see it now?

1618
01:20:05,687 --> 01:20:07,253
Hit the blockers' left hand.

1619
01:20:13,187 --> 01:20:14,353
Middle spike.

1620
01:20:14,353 --> 01:20:15,553
It's a touch-out.

1621
01:20:17,687 --> 01:20:19,887
The Kwangju Women's University players
are good.

1622
01:20:19,887 --> 01:20:21,087
Well done, guys.

1623
01:20:21,853 --> 01:20:23,253
Go with the flow of the ball.

1624
01:20:23,253 --> 01:20:24,487
Na Hee, go with the flow.

1625
01:20:25,720 --> 01:20:27,320
Na Hee!

1626
01:20:27,320 --> 01:20:29,720
Slide attack scores! Nice!

1627
01:20:30,120 --> 01:20:32,287
(An intense atmosphere)

1628
01:20:32,287 --> 01:20:34,220
I told you not to hold positions.

1629
01:20:34,653 --> 01:20:36,520
When we do, we open up space!

1630
01:20:36,520 --> 01:20:37,553
Move around and defend.

1631
01:20:37,787 --> 01:20:40,087
It's crucial not to let your guard down.

1632
01:20:40,087 --> 01:20:41,020
Right.

1633
01:20:41,020 --> 01:20:43,453
As Coach Yeon Koung mentioned earlier,

1634
01:20:43,453 --> 01:20:46,053
offensive efficiency isn't
Wonder Dogs' strongest suit.

1635
01:20:46,320 --> 01:20:47,653
Let's set it higher.

1636
01:20:50,020 --> 01:20:53,720
Keep your eyes on the setter.
Watch for the setters' tips.

1637
01:20:54,520 --> 01:20:56,987
Enkhsoyol, what did I tell you
when you don't have a good ball?

1638
01:20:56,987 --> 01:20:59,220
Tip it, or go deep. Right? Go deep.

1639
01:20:59,220 --> 01:21:00,053
Okay.

1640
01:21:01,387 --> 01:21:05,720
(They must raise their attack efficiency.)

1641
01:21:06,520 --> 01:21:08,553
(Seung Ju serving)

1642
01:21:11,653 --> 01:21:12,553
It hits the net.

1643
01:21:13,920 --> 01:21:14,753
Back set.

1644
01:21:15,287 --> 01:21:16,353
Dug!

1645
01:21:16,353 --> 01:21:17,387
Eun Jin!

1646
01:21:17,387 --> 01:21:18,587
Set it to Su Bin for the attack.

1647
01:21:22,180 --> 01:21:23,120
Powerful spike!

1648
01:21:23,543 --> 01:21:24,586
(Defending the number seven,)

1649
01:21:24,587 --> 01:21:25,720
They save it.

1650
01:21:25,720 --> 01:21:28,287
(Enkhsoyol is getting ready to attack.)

1651
01:21:29,187 --> 01:21:30,820
The set is a bit off.

1652
01:21:31,187 --> 01:21:32,953
What did I tell you
when you don't have a good ball?

1653
01:21:32,953 --> 01:21:34,220
Tip it, or go deep.

1654
01:21:34,953 --> 01:21:37,953
(Would she have gotten it this time?)

1655
01:21:43,953 --> 01:21:44,953
A long spike!

1656
01:21:45,387 --> 01:21:47,453
Enkhsoyol!

1657
01:21:51,953 --> 01:21:53,787
Enkhsoyol is on a roll today.

1658
01:21:53,787 --> 01:21:55,120
Yes, I like it.

1659
01:21:55,120 --> 01:21:59,387
She can hit more solidly
and break through.

1660
01:22:00,520 --> 01:22:02,453
The score is six to two,
a two-point difference.

1661
01:22:03,520 --> 01:22:04,753
Watch Enkhsoyol.

1662
01:22:06,287 --> 01:22:08,253
(Seung Ju serving)

1663
01:22:09,820 --> 01:22:10,787
Go!

1664
01:22:11,253 --> 01:22:12,553
Set the ball!

1665
01:22:12,553 --> 01:22:13,720
Go deep!

1666
01:22:15,553 --> 01:22:17,687
A roll shot to the left.

1667
01:22:17,687 --> 01:22:20,253
(Enkhsoyol gets ready for another attack.)

1668
01:22:20,920 --> 01:22:21,853
Spike!

1669
01:22:23,253 --> 01:22:24,853
Will it go out?

1670
01:22:28,953 --> 01:22:29,853
It's out!

1671
01:22:29,853 --> 01:22:31,587
Block out by Enkhsoyol!

1672
01:22:31,588 --> 01:22:34,499
(Block out point, thanks to Enkhsoyol!)

1673
01:22:35,020 --> 01:22:37,153
- Nice!
- Yes, that's it!

1674
01:22:37,587 --> 01:22:39,066
Nice, Enkhsoyol!

1675
01:22:43,253 --> 01:22:44,553
Good.

1676
01:22:47,344 --> 01:22:50,740
(Exclamation of joy)

1677
01:22:50,953 --> 01:22:53,287
Enkhsoyol looks so happy, smiling.

1678
01:22:53,287 --> 01:22:54,887
I feel like I'm going to cry.

1679
01:22:57,053 --> 01:22:59,720
Enkhsoyol with the brightest smile
we've ever seen.

1680
01:22:59,720 --> 01:23:01,153
(Her smile is no longer hidden
by worries.)

1681
01:23:01,387 --> 01:23:02,587
You can do it.

1682
01:23:02,887 --> 01:23:03,853
Give it your best shot.

1683
01:23:04,987 --> 01:23:06,920
I'll help you. Okay?

1684
01:23:06,920 --> 01:23:09,150
("I can't believe the Kim Yeon Koung is
coaching me.")

1685
01:23:09,151 --> 01:23:10,853
("I feel like I'm still dreaming.")

1686
01:23:10,854 --> 01:23:11,845
Serve.

1687
01:23:13,120 --> 01:23:16,787
(I felt stuck
and like I was never improving...)

1688
01:23:19,553 --> 01:23:25,687
("From Coach Kim: Hit forward
to drop it in, or run up and hit.")

1689
01:23:27,920 --> 01:23:33,453
("Back attack:
Get ready to shift up to the front.")

1690
01:23:35,587 --> 01:23:37,087
Watch out for Enkhsoyol!

1691
01:23:38,253 --> 01:23:39,153
They make the dig.

1692
01:23:43,087 --> 01:23:44,987
Soft roll shot by Enkhsoyol.

1693
01:23:44,987 --> 01:23:48,620
("If a tip from zone three isn't
available, push to the middle.")

1694
01:23:48,887 --> 01:23:51,953
(Great work, you're growing!)

1695
01:23:51,953 --> 01:23:54,187
When Enkhsoyol is on the right,
leave the straight open.

1696
01:23:56,453 --> 01:23:58,087
You can do it, Enkhsoyol!

1697
01:23:58,720 --> 01:24:00,687
Right-side spike!

1698
01:24:01,253 --> 01:24:04,853
(The sweet ache of growth)

1699
01:24:07,453 --> 01:24:09,587
Enkhsoyol!

1700
01:24:10,420 --> 01:24:12,120
(Nice job.)

1701
01:24:12,720 --> 01:24:13,853
Thank you.

1702
01:24:14,820 --> 01:24:18,420
("I'm so glad I didn't quit volleyball.")

1703
01:24:18,653 --> 01:24:22,287
Enkhsoyol is brimming with confidence,
since this is against a university.

1704
01:24:22,287 --> 01:24:24,820
She definitely looks
more confident than usual.

1705
01:24:24,820 --> 01:24:27,420
- You can see that from her face too.
- Yes.

1706
01:24:28,087 --> 01:24:30,087
(The new ace)

1707
01:24:31,353 --> 01:24:32,887
(Still working to become one)

1708
01:24:34,320 --> 01:24:35,287
All right.

1709
01:24:38,320 --> 01:24:40,320
Now, 12 to 10.

1710
01:24:40,753 --> 01:24:42,287
- Go deep.
- Okay.

1711
01:24:43,187 --> 01:24:46,020
(Enkhsoyol is still growing.)

1712
01:24:47,712 --> 01:24:48,946
(To stop consecutive losses,)

1713
01:24:49,102 --> 01:24:50,179
(Enkhsoyol's getting in the zone.)

1714
01:24:50,179 --> 01:24:51,179
(From offense...)

1715
01:24:51,179 --> 01:24:53,146
(to defense)

1716
01:24:53,446 --> 01:24:54,846
(Enkhsoyol is the new ace today!)

1717
01:24:54,846 --> 01:24:57,312
We all know their play style, don't we?

1718
01:24:57,312 --> 01:24:58,979
So let's play more aggressively.

1719
01:24:58,979 --> 01:24:59,946
(Analysis done.)

1720
01:24:59,946 --> 01:25:01,112
(Time to attack)

1721
01:25:01,479 --> 01:25:02,412
(Young bloods counterattack,)

1722
01:25:02,679 --> 01:25:03,612
(and the older players...)

1723
01:25:03,612 --> 01:25:04,812
(are getting helpless.)

1724
01:25:06,379 --> 01:25:07,379
(Counterattack complete)

1725
01:25:09,112 --> 01:25:10,446
I talked to the producer.

1726
01:25:10,446 --> 01:25:12,279
I suggested we should release players.

1727
01:25:12,546 --> 01:25:14,079
Let the players go.

1728
01:25:14,079 --> 01:25:16,346
(A drastic measure by the rookie coach)

1729
01:25:16,746 --> 01:25:19,612
(Will the Wonder Dogs start a cut system?)

1730
01:25:19,612 --> 01:25:20,746
We're done here.
